{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Q6HvwPZGDzEBYqydBRDyU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  CIVO mechanism confirmed in DMC locomotion (Walker Walk + Cheetah Run) with gradient-level\n  causal evidence (Full-SGS NVE=1.00×). NVE>1.5x threshold achieves perfect separation in Walker\n  (4/4) and near-perfect in Cheetah (5/6 or 6/6). Cartpole Swingup results are 'consistent with\n  but do not independently confirm' the mechanism — NVE stays in gray zone or only borderline\n  exceeds threshold, preventing a clean third-environment confirmation. Scope primary findings to\n  RSSM + proprioceptive DMC locomotion; discuss Cartpole as preliminary extension showing\n  degradation without unambiguous CIVO signature. Weaken 'generalizes across environments' to\n  'generalizes within DMC locomotion; further investigation needed for non-locomotion/visual\n  domains'. Pathway B (non-CIVO policy instability from trained dt_emb) remains under-characterized\n  — 2/4 seeds collapse across 008e_v3, mechanism identified (eval-driven, entropy↑) but causal\n  chain incomplete. Paper publishable at CoRL as strong 2-environment mechanistic diagnosis +\n  practical warning + novel TAWM contrast (MPC success vs imagination failure).\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # WALKER WALK — Multi-seed replication\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"Replicate CIVO collapse with 2 additional seeds for 008d (subsample ON + trained dt_emb + H=8)\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_009e:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 167, 35K: 146, 45K: 141, 55K: 83, 65K: 250, 75K: 178, 85K: 202, 95K: 133, 105K: 131}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 1.78, 35K: 1.71, 45K: 2.09, 55K: 4.12, 65K: 1.23, 75K: 1.48, 85K: 1.15, 95K: 1.73, 105K: 1.57}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: true\n        collapse: true\n        collapse_onset_step: 25K\n        peak_nve: 4.12\n        final_eval: 131\n      seed2_009b:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 141, 35K: 164, 45K: 141, 55K: 172, 65K: 209, 75K: 197, 85K: 236, 95K: 279, 105K: 268}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 2.05, 35K: 1.24, 45K: 1.62, 55K: 1.41, 65K: 0.94, 75K: 0.66, 85K: 0.51, 95K: 0.43, 105K: 0.38}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: true  # 1.62x@45K\n        collapse: false\n        value_self_correction: true\n        value_peak: 110.9\n        value_peak_step: 65K\n        final_eval: 268\n      combined:\n        nve_above_1_5x_rate: \"2/2\"\n        collapse_rate: \"1/2\"\n        independent_collapse_rate: 0.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档位下，Walker Walk 中 trained dt_emb 可靠触发 nve>1.5x（2/2 seeds 均超阈值），\n      但崩溃是随机的（1/2）。Seed 1 的 RSSM 在 dt=2 处产生系统性 reward 偏差（reward gap 2.78x），\n      trained dt_emb 让 critic 精确利用这个偏差，形成 value→actor→data→value 正反馈。Seed 2 同样\n      触发 nve>1.5x，但早期训练随机性（初始化、数据采样顺序）使得过度估计未能在连续 3 个 checkpoint\n      持续超过 1.5x，actor 仍能从 real returns 获得纠正梯度，value 自修正。这与 Henderson et al. 2018\n      和 Bjorck et al. 2022 的早期随机性决定训练轨迹一致。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"NVE threshold classification (Walker trained dt_emb)\"\n        data: |\n          | Seed | nve>1.5x at 35K+ | Collapse | Peak NVE | Sustained >1.5x |\n          |------|------------------|----------|----------|-----------------|\n          | 0 (008d) | ✓ (1.71x@35K) | ✓ | 4.12x | 3 checkpoints |\n          | 1 (009e) | ✓ (1.71x@35K) | ✓ | 4.12x | 3 checkpoints |\n          | 2 (009b) | ✓ (1.62x@45K) | ✗ | 2.05x | 1 checkpoint |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Learning curves: 008d seed 0+1 (collapse) vs 009b seed 2 (self-correction), overlaid with baseline\"\n      - \"NVE trajectories: 3 seeds showing all exceed 1.5x but diverge in persistence\"\n    analysis: >\n      nve>1.5x 阈值在 trained dt_emb 条件下达到 3/3（含 seed 0）完美检出率。崩溃概率 2/3\n      （seed 0 和 seed 1 崩溃，seed 2 自修正）。关键发现：sustained nve>1.5x（连续 3+\n      checkpoints）是区分崩溃 vs 自修正的第二道门。论文报告 nve>1.5x 为 necessary condition，\n      temporal persistence 为 collapse gate。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control stability with 2 additional seeds (subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8)\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_009f:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 185, 35K: 210, 45K: 195, 55K: 230, 65K: 310, 75K: 280, 85K: 350, 95K: 310, 105K: 420}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 0.95, 35K: 0.75, 45K: 0.80, 55K: 0.88, 65K: 0.45, 75K: 0.50, 85K: 0.55, 95K: 0.48, 105K: 0.35}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: false\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 420\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-54.1%\"\n      seed2_009c:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 169, 35K: 179, 45K: 211, 55K: 239, 65K: 244, 75K: 359, 85K: 227, 95K: 191, 105K: 148}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 1.26, 35K: 0.79, 45K: 0.72, 55K: 0.66, 65K: 0.53, 75K: 0.33, 85K: 0.60, 95K: 0.90, 105K: 1.14}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: false\n        collapse: false  # performance degrades but not CIVO-driven\n        final_eval: 148\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-83.8%\"\n        note: \"Decline after 75K but nve stays <1.5x; NOT delusional critic but learning instability without dt conditioning\"\n      combined:\n        nve_above_1_5x_rate: \"0/2\"\n        collapse_rate: \"0/2\"\n        cross_seed_consistency: \"Low — seed 1 recovers to 420, seed 2 declines to 148\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      去掉 dt_embedding 后，reward head 无法区分 dt=1/dt=2（reward gap 仅 1.01x），阻断了\n      CIVO 正反馈环。两个 seed 的 nve 均未超过 1.5x（max 1.26x@25K for seed 2，属于 early-stage\n      false positive zone）。但 008f 配置本身牺牲了 reward 预测质量（MAE 为 baseline 75x），\n      导致跨 seed 一致性差——seed 1 zigzag 恢复到 420（类似 seed 0 的 503），seed 2 则在 75K\n      后持续下降到 148。这种高方差归因于 reward head 噪声使 actor 学习信号质量不稳定。\n      关键论点不变：008f 是因果控制实验证明 \"without dt_emb → no CIVO\"，不是推荐方案。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"NVE threshold classification (Walker no dt_emb)\"\n        data: |\n          | Seed | nve>1.5x at 35K+ | Collapse | Peak NVE (35K+) | Final eval |\n          |------|------------------|----------|-----------------|------------|\n          | 0 (008f) | ✗ (0.97x) | ✗ | 0.97x | 503 |\n          | 1 (009f) | ✗ (0.88x) | ✗ | 0.88x | 420 |\n          | 2 (009c) | ✗ (1.14x) | ✗ | 1.14x | 148 |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"NVE trajectories: 3 seeds all below 1.5x, contrasted with 008d 3 seeds all above 1.5x\"\n    analysis: >\n      Combined with plan_011: NVE>1.5x threshold achieves 6/6 perfect classification in Walker\n      (3/3 trained exceed, 3/3 no-dt-emb below). 008f seed 2 的 nve=1.14x@105K 是最接近阈值的\n      case，但仍有 24% margin。论文中可报告 008f 跨 seed 高方差（148-503）作为 \"因果控制的代价\"，\n      与 008e_v3 seed 1 (869.9) 对比突出后者更实用。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression and zigzag recovery with 2 additional seeds (subsample OFF + untrained dt_emb + H=15)\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory: {35K: 460, 45K: 520, 55K: 440, 65K: 570, 75K: 500, 85K: 560, 95K: 610, 105K: 710}\n        nve_trajectory: {55K: 0.85, 65K: 0.62, 75K: 0.70, 85K: 0.65, 95K: 0.72, 105K: 0.55}\n        final_eval: 710\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-22.5%\"\n        zigzag_recovery: true\n        n_recovery_cycles: 2\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory: {35K: 420, 45K: 480, 55K: 410, 65K: 530, 75K: 450, 85K: 520, 95K: 550, 105K: 660}\n        nve_trajectory: {55K: 0.80, 65K: 0.58, 75K: 0.68, 85K: 0.63, 95K: 0.70, 105K: 0.52}\n        final_eval: 660\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-27.9%\"\n        zigzag_recovery: true\n        n_recovery_cycles: 2\n      combined:\n        iqm_105K: 716  # (778 + 710 + 660) / 3\n        iqm_vs_baseline: \"-21.8%\"\n        nve_range_105K: [0.52, 0.59]\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Untrained dt_emb 使 value function 无法利用精确的 dt>1 预测信息——dt_embedding 是随机固定的，\n      对 critic 来说 dt=1 和 dt=2 的 conditioning 没有语义区分。这从源头阻断了 CIVO 正反馈。\n      Median 档位下，两个新 seed 复现 seed 0 的 zigzag recovery 模式（V-shaped dips + recoveries），\n      但绝对水平略低于 seed 0（710, 660 vs 778）——这是 untrained dt_emb 配置的典型高方差特征。\n      nve 在所有 seed 中均被压制在 0.52-0.93x range，随时间进一步远离 baseline（结构性抑制，\n      非暂时延迟）。关键差异：这些 seed 的 recovery cycles 可能在 timing 上不同步，但 pattern\n      （dip → recovery → dip → higher recovery）一致，说明 zigzag 是配置的内在特征而非随机波动。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008a cross-seed summary\"\n        data: |\n          | Seed | eval@105K | nve@105K | V-recoveries | vs baseline |\n          |------|-----------|----------|--------------|-------------|\n          | 0    | 778       | 0.59x    | 2 cycles     | -15.1%      |\n          | 1    | 710       | 0.55x    | 2 cycles     | -22.5%      |\n          | 2    | 660       | 0.52x    | 2 cycles     | -27.9%      |\n          | IQM  | 716       | 0.55x    | —            | -21.8%      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-seed learning curves with shaded IQM confidence band, showing consistent zigzag pattern\"\n      - \"NVE trajectories: all 3 seeds consistently below 1.0x and declining\"\n    analysis: >\n      3-seed 数据确认 untrained dt_emb 的 value suppression 是 robust 的（0/3 collapse，nve\n      range 0.52-0.59x@105K）。IQM 716 (78% baseline) 低于 seed 0 的 778 (85%)，报告时使用\n      IQM + 95% CI 而非 best seed。C3 claim strength 保持 Strong。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 (dt=1 imag) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"Multi-seed validation of trained dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=1 imagination + H=15\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_s1:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 156, 35K: 276, 45K: 382, 55K: 487, 65K: 581, 75K: 574, 85K: 657, 95K: 852, 105K: 870}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 0.94, 45K: 0.88, 55K: 0.87, 65K: 0.72, 75K: 0.73, 85K: 0.76, 95K: 0.75, 105K: 0.80}\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 870\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-5.0%\"\n        pathway: \"healthy\"\n      seed2_s2:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 212, 35K: 320, 45K: 357, 55K: 418, 65K: 435, 75K: 577, 85K: 715, 95K: 452, 105K: 137}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 1.03, 45K: 1.06, 55K: 1.02, 65K: 0.90, 75K: 0.66, 85K: 0.68, 95K: 1.34, 105K: 3.78}\n        collapse: true\n        collapse_onset: 95K\n        collapse_type: \"Pathway B (non-CIVO, eval-driven, entropy↑)\"\n        actor_entropy_at_collapse: {85K: -5.21, 95K: -4.53, 105K: -3.83}\n        final_eval: 137\n        gate_dt_1_frac: 1.0  # dt=1 imagination never violated\n      combined:\n        collapse_rate: \"1/2\"\n        pathway_A_civo: \"0/2 (eliminated by dt=1 imagination)\"\n        pathway_B_non_civo: \"1/2\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      dt=1 imagination 消除了 Pathway A (CIVO)——imagination rollout 中不产生 dt>1 transitions，\n      critic 不会在 dt>1 处累积 overestimation。但 training data 仍含 dt>1 transitions（subsample ON），\n      trained dt_emb 仍在学习 dt=1 vs dt=2 的区分。Seed 2 的崩溃走 Pathway B：eval 先崩\n      （715→452→137），value 相对稳定（339→384→340），nve 被 eval 分母驱动而非 value 分子驱动。\n      actor_entropy 上升（-5.21→-3.83）是策略去确定化的信号，与 CIVO 的 entropy↓ 相反。\n      009a baseline s2 在同期完全稳定（618→596→836），排除 seed 2 固有脆弱假说。\n      Median 档下 Pathway B 的确切机制未完全刻画——可能是 trained dt_emb 在 representation 层面\n      引入的干扰（93% 梯度来自 observation decoders），但因果链不如 Pathway A 清晰。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008e_v3 Pathway A vs Pathway B\"\n        data: |\n          | Feature        | 008d s0 (Pathway A) | 008e_v3 s2 (Pathway B) |\n          |----------------|---------------------|------------------------|\n          | value Δ        | +130% (60→138)      | +13% (339→384)         |\n          | eval Δ         | -43% (146→83)       | -81% (715→137)         |\n          | nve driver     | value numerator     | eval denominator       |\n          | actor_entropy  | ↓ (-3.47→-4.88)     | ↑ (-5.21→-3.83)       |\n          | dt in imag     | dt=2                | dt=1 (never violated)  |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Side-by-side: 008e_v3 seed 1 (healthy) vs seed 2 (Pathway B collapse)\"\n      - \"Actor entropy comparison: CIVO collapse (↓) vs Pathway B collapse (↑)\"\n    analysis: >\n      C6 partially falsified：dt=1 imagination 消除 Pathway A 但不消除 Pathway B。崩溃率 1/2\n      与 008d (1/2-2/3) 相当——dt=1 imagination 未降低总崩溃概率。论文需将 C6 从 \"practical\n      mitigation\" 改为 \"partial mitigation (eliminates CIVO pathway only)\"。Pathway B 作为\n      open question 在 Discussion 中报告。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=2 + H=8\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"Freeze dt_embedding (requires_grad=False, random init). Diagnostic: is dt_emb TRAINING the necessary condition for CIVO?\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 172, 35K: 202, 45K: 122, 55K: 106, 65K: 160, 75K: 80, 85K: 184, 95K: 238, 105K: 204}\n        nve_trajectory: {85K: 0.47, 95K: 0.39, 105K: 0.42}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x: false\n        collapse: false\n        collapse_mechanism: \"gradient_starvation — actor_loss→0 due to frozen conditioning\"\n        actor_loss_105K: 0.000179\n        actor_entropy_105K: -4.855\n        value_mean_105K: 56.2\n        gate_dt_mean: 2.0\n        final_eval: 204\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-77.7%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Frozen dt_emb 是一个不同的失败模式：dt_embedding 固定在随机值，gate 输出恒定 dt=2，\n      但 embedding 永远不更新以匹配 RSSM dynamics。结果是 critic 收到的 conditioning 信号\n      与 state transitions 不一致，但不会产生 CIVO 的正反馈（因为 embedding 不被训练去\n      exploit RSSM 的 systematic bias）。NVE 远低于 1.0x（0.39-0.47x，critic under-estimates），\n      actor_loss→0 说明 value gradient 无法有效驱动 policy improvement。这是 gradient starvation，\n      不是 value overestimation。\n      关键论点：frozen dt_emb 确认 CIVO 需要 dt_emb 的 TRAINING——是训练过程中 observation\n      decoder 梯度（93%）塑造 dt_embedding 以 exploit RSSM fidelity gap 的能力导致了 CIVO，\n      而非 dt_embedding 的存在本身。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"dt_emb condition × CIVO outcome (Walker 2×2 matrix)\"\n        data: |\n          | dt_emb state      | Config     | NVE range  | CIVO? | Outcome         |\n          |-------------------|------------|------------|-------|-----------------|\n          | Trained           | 008d       | 1.7-4.1x   | ✓     | Collapse (2/3)  |\n          | Frozen (random)   | 015b       | 0.39-0.47x | ✗     | Grad starvation |\n          | Absent (dim=0)    | 008f       | 0.30-0.97x | ✗     | Zigzag recovery |\n          | Untrained (OFF)   | 008a       | 0.52-0.93x | ✗     | Zigzag recovery |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-way comparison: trained / frozen / absent / unexposed dt_emb learning curves\"\n    analysis: >\n      2×2 消融矩阵闭合：只有 trained + exposed to dt>1 data 的 dt_emb 触发 CIVO。Frozen 和\n      absent 都不触发，但通过不同机制失败（gradient starvation vs reward degradation）。\n      这强化了 C2: dt_emb TRAINING（而非 dt_emb 存在）是 CIVO 的 necessary condition。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 additional seeds (seed 3-4)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"Narrow 008e_v3 collapse rate estimate with 2 additional seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed3:\n        eval_trajectory: {35K: 290, 45K: 400, 55K: 510, 65K: 590, 75K: 620, 85K: 700, 95K: 820, 105K: 845}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 0.90, 45K: 0.85, 55K: 0.82, 65K: 0.70, 75K: 0.68, 85K: 0.72, 95K: 0.70, 105K: 0.75}\n        collapse: false\n        pathway: \"healthy\"\n        final_eval: 845\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-7.7%\"\n      seed4:\n        eval_trajectory: {35K: 260, 45K: 370, 55K: 450, 65K: 530, 75K: 580, 85K: 680, 95K: 420, 105K: 180}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 0.98, 45K: 0.90, 55K: 0.85, 65K: 0.75, 75K: 0.70, 85K: 0.73, 95K: 1.40, 105K: 3.20}\n        collapse: true\n        collapse_onset: 95K\n        collapse_type: \"Pathway B (non-CIVO)\"\n        actor_entropy_at_collapse: {85K: -5.15, 95K: -4.40, 105K: -3.65}\n        final_eval: 180\n      combined_all_4_seeds:\n        collapse_rate: \"2/4 (50%)\"\n        pathway_A_count: 0\n        pathway_B_count: 2\n        healthy_count: 2\n        iqm_healthy_seeds: 858  # (870 + 845) / 2\n        collapse_onset_range: \"95-105K\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档位下，008e_v3 的崩溃率稳定在 ~50%（2/4 seeds）。所有崩溃都走 Pathway B（eval-driven,\n      entropy↑），没有 Pathway A (CIVO) 出现——dt=1 imagination 有效消除了 value-driven 崩溃。\n      Pathway B 的 onset 一致在 90-100K range，晚于 Pathway A 的 25-35K onset ~70K steps。\n      这说明 Pathway B 是 slower-developing vulnerability，可能与 trained dt_emb 在 representation\n      space 中引入的 subtle bias 有关（93% 梯度来自 observation decoders 在持续塑造 dt_emb，\n      即使 imagination 不使用 dt>1）。4 seeds 不足以精确估计 collapse rate 的 CI，但 2/4\n      与 008d 的 2/3 相当，说明 dt=1 imagination 没有显著降低总崩溃概率。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008e_v3 4-seed summary\"\n        data: |\n          | Seed | eval@105K | Collapse | Pathway | Onset   |\n          |------|-----------|----------|---------|---------|\n          | 1    | 870       | ✗        | healthy | —       |\n          | 2    | 137       | ✓        | B       | 95K     |\n          | 3    | 845       | ✗        | healthy | —       |\n          | 4    | 180       | ✓        | B       | 95K     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-seed learning curves, color-coded by collapse/healthy\"\n      - \"Collapse rate comparison: 008d (2/3 CIVO) vs 008e_v3 (2/4 Pathway B)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Pathway B 在 Median 档下仍是 under-characterized。2/4 = 50% 崩溃率的 binomial 95% CI\n      是 [15%, 85%]——需要更多 seeds 才能精确估计。但方向性结论稳固：trained dt_emb + dt=1\n      imagination 不是 safe 配置。论文中 acknowledge \"Pathway B mechanism requires further\n      investigation\" 并将其作为 future work。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # CHEETAH RUN — Cross-environment replication\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in second DMC environment, establishing reference performance and v/e calibration\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 280, 45K: 480, 65K: 620, 85K: 720, 105K: 790, 155K: 830, 205K: 845, 305K: 855, 505K: 860}\n        ve_ratio_trajectory: {25K: 0.10, 45K: 0.28, 65K: 0.45, 85K: 0.58, 105K: 0.64, 155K: 0.68, 205K: 0.70}\n        peak_eval: 860\n        ve_stable_range: \"0.68-0.72 from 155K+\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 260, 45K: 460, 65K: 600, 85K: 700, 105K: 770, 155K: 820, 205K: 840, 505K: 850}\n        peak_eval: 850  # matches exp_010a actual data\n        ve_stable_range: \"0.67-0.71\"\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 300, 45K: 500, 65K: 640, 85K: 730, 105K: 800, 155K: 835, 205K: 850, 505K: 855}\n        peak_eval: 855\n        ve_stable_range: \"0.69-0.73\"\n      combined:\n        iqm_peak: 847\n        iqm_105K: 787\n        ve_stable_cross_seed: \"0.68-0.72\"\n        convergence_step: \"~155K (90% of asymptotic)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah Run 是 DMC locomotion suite 中第二标准环境。DreamerV3 在 Cheetah Run 上的 asymptotic\n      performance 略低于 Walker Walk（~850 vs ~950），因为 Cheetah 的 reward signal 更密集但\n      动力学更复杂（更多自由度的关节）。v/e calibration 与 Walker 相近（stable ~68-72%），\n      说明 DreamerV3 的 value function 在 proprioceptive DMC 任务上有一致的 overestimation\n      profile。这为 Cheetah 的 NVE 计算提供了 denominator。Seed 1 与 exp_010a 实际数据一致（849.8）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah baseline cross-seed\"\n        data: |\n          | Seed | eval@105K | Peak eval | v/e stable |\n          |------|-----------|-----------|------------|\n          | 0    | 790       | 860       | 0.68-0.72  |\n          | 1    | 770       | 850       | 0.67-0.71  |\n          | 2    | 800       | 855       | 0.69-0.73  |\n          | IQM  | 787       | 847       | 0.68-0.72  |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah baseline 3-seed learning curves with IQM band\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 稳健，cross-seed 方差小（peak range 850-860）。v/e calibration 一致。\n      为 Cheetah CIVO 实验提供可靠 reference。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: \"Replicate CIVO in Cheetah Run — key cross-environment validation\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory: {15K: 180, 25K: 320, 35K: 410, 45K: 380, 55K: 280, 65K: 150, 75K: 120}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 1.40, 35K: 1.82, 45K: 2.15, 55K: 2.48, 65K: 3.50}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: true\n        collapse: true\n        collapse_onset: 35K\n        peak_eval: 410\n        final_eval: 120\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory: {15K: 165, 25K: 290, 35K: 380, 45K: 350, 55K: 320, 65K: 350, 75K: 280, 85K: 310, 95K: 340, 105K: 370}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 1.30, 35K: 1.65, 45K: 1.48, 55K: 1.20, 65K: 0.95, 75K: 0.80, 85K: 0.72, 95K: 0.65, 105K: 0.58}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: true  # 1.65x@35K\n        collapse: false\n        value_self_correction: true\n        final_eval: 370\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-53.0%\"\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory: {15K: 190, 25K: 340, 35K: 430, 45K: 400, 55K: 310, 65K: 170, 75K: 95}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 1.50, 35K: 1.95, 45K: 2.30, 55K: 2.80, 65K: 4.10}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: true\n        collapse: true\n        collapse_onset: 35K\n        peak_eval: 430\n        final_eval: 95\n      combined:\n        nve_above_1_5x_rate: \"3/3\"\n        collapse_rate: \"2/3\"\n        cross_env_civo_collapse_rate: 0.33  # within [0.25, 0.5]\n        cheetah_civo_nve_35K_plus_range: [1.65, 2.48]  # within [1.5, 2.5]\n        iqm_all_seeds: ~195  # heavily dragged by collapsed seeds\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档位的核心预测：Cheetah 干净复制 Walker 的 CIVO 现象。RSSM 在 Cheetah 的 dt>1\n      prediction fidelity gap 与 Walker 类似（proprioceptive observations, continuous control），\n      trained dt_emb 同样触发 value overestimation feedback loop。3/3 seeds 的 nve 在 35K+\n      均超过 1.5x（range 1.65-2.48x，在 median 档的 [1.5, 2.5] 内）。崩溃率 2/3（0.33，\n      在 [0.25, 0.5] 内）。Seed 1 类似 Walker 009b 的自修正模式——nve 短暂超过 1.5x 后\n      回落。Cheetah 的 collapse onset（35K）与 Walker（25-35K）timing 相近，支持 \"RSSM\n      fidelity gap 在 35K 左右积累到临界水平\" 的机制假说。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah CIVO cross-seed\"\n        data: |\n          | Seed | nve@35K | nve@45K | Peak NVE | Collapse | Final eval |\n          |------|---------|---------|----------|----------|------------|\n          | 0    | 1.82x   | 2.15x   | 3.50x    | ✓        | 120        |\n          | 1    | 1.65x   | 1.48x   | 1.65x    | ✗        | 370        |\n          | 2    | 1.95x   | 2.30x   | 4.10x    | ✓        | 95         |\n      - name: \"Cross-environment CIVO comparison\"\n        data: |\n          | Env     | nve>1.5x rate | Collapse rate | Peak NVE range | Onset |\n          |---------|---------------|---------------|----------------|-------|\n          | Walker  | 3/3           | 2/3           | 2.05-4.12x     | 25-35K|\n          | Cheetah | 3/3           | 2/3           | 1.65-4.10x     | 35K   |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah 3-seed CIVO learning curves, overlaid with Walker 008d for cross-env comparison\"\n      - \"NVE trajectories: Cheetah 3 seeds, with 1.5x threshold line\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 复制是论文最重要的新增证据。nve>1.5x 阈值在 Cheetah 也实现 3/3 检出。\n      Combined Walker + Cheetah: trained dt_emb 6/6 超 1.5x (100%)。论文可 claim \"CIVO\n      mechanism confirmed in DMC locomotion\"。崩溃率跨环境一致 (~50-67%)，支持 \"CIVO 是\n      necessary condition, collapse stochastic\" 的叙事。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control (no dt_embedding → no CIVO) in Cheetah Run\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 170, 35K: 200, 45K: 220, 55K: 240, 65K: 300, 75K: 280, 85K: 310, 95K: 350, 105K: 380}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 0.90, 35K: 0.70, 45K: 0.75, 55K: 0.82, 65K: 0.50, 75K: 0.55, 85K: 0.60, 95K: 0.52, 105K: 0.45}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: false\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 380\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-51.9%\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 155, 35K: 190, 45K: 210, 55K: 195, 65K: 260, 75K: 240, 85K: 270, 95K: 300, 105K: 330}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 0.80, 45K: 0.68, 55K: 0.90, 65K: 0.55, 85K: 0.70, 105K: 0.55}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: false\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 330\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 180, 35K: 215, 45K: 240, 55K: 260, 65K: 320, 75K: 310, 85K: 340, 95K: 370, 105K: 400}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 0.65, 45K: 0.72, 55K: 0.78, 65K: 0.48, 85K: 0.58, 105K: 0.40}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: false\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 400\n      combined:\n        nve_above_1_5x_rate: \"0/3\"\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n        cheetah_no_dt_emb_nve_35K_plus_range: [0.40, 0.90]  # within [0.4, 1.1]\n        iqm_105K: 370\n        vs_baseline_iqm: \"-53.0%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 Walker 008f 的模式一致：去掉 dt_embedding 后 reward head 无法区分 dt=1/dt=2，\n      阻断 CIVO 正反馈。所有 3 seeds 的 nve 在 35K+ 范围内为 0.40-0.90x（在 median 档的\n      [0.4, 1.1] 内），无 seed 超过 1.5x。性能损失约 50%（与 Walker 008f 的 45-84% 损失\n      range 一致），归因于 reward prediction degradation。Cheetah 与 Walker 的因果控制\n      结论一致：no dt_emb → no CIVO。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah no-dt-emb cross-seed\"\n        data: |\n          | Seed | nve max (35K+) | Collapse | eval@105K | vs baseline |\n          |------|----------------|----------|-----------|-------------|\n          | 0    | 0.82x          | ✗        | 380       | -51.9%      |\n          | 1    | 0.90x          | ✗        | 330       | -58.2%      |\n          | 2    | 0.78x          | ✗        | 400       | -49.4%      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah no-dt-emb NVE trajectories contrasted with trained dt_emb (plan_021)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Combined with plan_021: Cheetah NVE threshold classification = 6/6 (3/3 trained exceed,\n      3/3 no-dt-emb below). Cross-environment NVE threshold total: Walker 6/6 + Cheetah 6/6\n      = 12/12 (100%). 论文可 claim \"NVE>1.5x is a reliable cross-environment diagnostic\n      for trained dt_emb CIVO in DMC locomotion\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression pattern in Cheetah\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory: {35K: 380, 45K: 440, 55K: 400, 65K: 490, 75K: 460, 85K: 520, 95K: 540, 105K: 620}\n        nve_trajectory: {55K: 0.78, 65K: 0.60, 75K: 0.65, 85K: 0.62, 95K: 0.68, 105K: 0.55}\n        final_eval: 620\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-21.4%\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory: {35K: 350, 45K: 410, 55K: 380, 65K: 460, 75K: 430, 85K: 490, 95K: 510, 105K: 580}\n        nve_trajectory: {55K: 0.82, 65K: 0.63, 75K: 0.70, 85K: 0.65, 95K: 0.72, 105K: 0.58}\n        final_eval: 580\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-26.5%\"\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory: {35K: 400, 45K: 470, 55K: 420, 65K: 520, 75K: 490, 85K: 550, 95K: 570, 105K: 650}\n        nve_trajectory: {55K: 0.75, 65K: 0.57, 75K: 0.63, 85K: 0.60, 95K: 0.65, 105K: 0.52}\n        final_eval: 650\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-17.6%\"\n      combined:\n        iqm_105K: 617\n        vs_baseline_iqm: \"-21.8%\"\n        nve_range_105K: [0.52, 0.58]\n        zigzag_recovery: \"2/3 seeds show at least 1 V-recovery cycle\"\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 Walker 008a 模式一致：untrained dt_emb 阻断 CIVO 但保留了完整的 model architecture\n      （包括 dt_embedding 参数，只是不更新权重 exposed to dt>1 data）。Value function 无法\n      exploit dt-specific conditioning，nve 被压制在 0.52-0.82x range。Zigzag recovery 模式\n      在 Cheetah 中也出现，但幅度可能略小（Cheetah 的 observation space 更大，learning 更\n      noisy）。IQM 617 (78% baseline) 与 Walker 008a 的 IQM 716 (78% baseline) 百分比一致，\n      说明 untrained dt_emb 的 \"代价\" 是跨环境稳定的 ~20% performance loss。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah untrained dt_emb learning curves, contrasted with trained (plan_021) and no-dt-emb (plan_022)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 确认 untrained dt_emb 的 value suppression 是跨环境 robust 的。\n      与 plan_021/022 合并：Cheetah 完整复制 Walker 的 CIVO 因果链。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # CARTPOLE SWINGUP — Third environment (borderline in median)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_050\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in non-locomotion DMC environment\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 300, 45K: 540, 65K: 680, 85K: 760, 105K: 800, 155K: 830, 205K: 845, 505K: 855}\n        peak_eval: 855\n        ve_stable_range: \"0.65-0.70\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 280, 45K: 520, 65K: 660, 85K: 740, 105K: 790, 155K: 825, 505K: 850}\n        peak_eval: 850\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 320, 45K: 560, 65K: 700, 85K: 770, 105K: 810, 155K: 840, 505K: 860}\n        peak_eval: 860\n      combined:\n        iqm_peak: 855\n        iqm_105K: 800\n        ve_stable_cross_seed: \"0.65-0.71\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole Swingup 是 DMC 非 locomotion 任务。DreamerV3 在此环境 asymptotic ~850-860，\n      略低于 Walker (~950) 但与 Cheetah 相近。v/e calibration 与 locomotion 任务相似\n      （0.65-0.71），说明 DreamerV3 的 value overestimation profile 在 proprioceptive\n      DMC 任务间相对一致。Cartpole 的 observation space 比 locomotion 更简单（仅 cart position,\n      velocity, pole angle, angular velocity），这可能影响 RSSM 在 dt>1 处的 fidelity gap\n      大小——简单 dynamics 可能让 RSSM 在 dt>1 处也能保持较好精度。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole baseline 3-seed learning curves\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 稳健。关键不确定性：Cartpole 更简单的 dynamics 是否会减小 RSSM fidelity gap，\n      从而削弱 CIVO 的 intensity。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_051\"\n    description: \"Test CIVO in non-locomotion DMC environment\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory: {15K: 160, 25K: 310, 35K: 420, 45K: 380, 55K: 350, 65K: 320, 75K: 290, 85K: 280, 95K: 270, 105K: 260}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 1.20, 35K: 1.42, 45K: 1.55, 55K: 1.48, 65K: 1.35, 75K: 1.30, 85K: 1.25, 95K: 1.20, 105K: 1.15}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: true  # 1.55x@45K but transient\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 260\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-67.5%\"\n        note: \"NVE briefly exceeds 1.5x at 45K but does not sustain\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory: {15K: 150, 25K: 290, 35K: 400, 45K: 370, 55K: 340, 65K: 310, 75K: 350, 85K: 320, 95K: 340, 105K: 310}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 1.10, 35K: 1.35, 45K: 1.40, 55K: 1.32, 65K: 1.25, 75K: 1.10, 85K: 1.05, 95K: 1.00, 105K: 0.95}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: false  # max 1.40x — below threshold\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 310\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory: {15K: 170, 25K: 330, 35K: 440, 45K: 410, 55K: 350, 65K: 180, 75K: 140}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 1.30, 35K: 1.60, 45K: 1.85, 55K: 2.10, 65K: 2.80}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: true\n        collapse: true\n        collapse_onset: 45K\n        final_eval: 140\n      combined:\n        nve_above_1_5x_rate: \"2/3\"\n        collapse_rate: \"1/3\"\n        nve_35K_plus_range: [0.95, 2.80]\n        threshold_1_5x_classification: \"2/3 correctly classified (seed 1 = false negative: trained dt_emb but nve<1.5x)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档位下 Cartpole 的 CIVO 表现不如 locomotion 任务清晰。原因：Cartpole 的 dynamics\n      更简单（4-dim state vs Walker 的 24-dim），RSSM 在 dt>1 处的 prediction error 较小，\n      导致 reward gap ratio 不如 Walker/Cheetah 大。结果是 nve 整体偏低（部分 seed 的 nve\n      在 1.3-1.5x 的灰色地带），1.5x 阈值在 Cartpole 上出现 false negative（seed 1 有\n      trained dt_emb 但 nve 仅 1.40x）。只有 1/3 seeds 崩溃——相比 Walker/Cheetah 的 ~50-67%\n      明显更低。这导致 Cartpole 不能被计入 \"confirmed CIVO\" 环境，只能说 \"consistent with CIVO\n      but threshold may need environment-specific calibration\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole CIVO cross-seed\"\n        data: |\n          | Seed | nve max (35K+) | >1.5x? | Collapse | Final eval |\n          |------|----------------|--------|----------|------------|\n          | 0    | 1.55x          | ✓ (transient) | ✗ | 260        |\n          | 1    | 1.40x          | ✗ (gray zone) | ✗ | 310        |\n          | 2    | 2.80x          | ✓      | ✓        | 140        |\n      - name: \"NVE threshold accuracy: cross-environment\"\n        data: |\n          | Env       | Trained (>1.5x?) | No-dt-emb (<1.5x?) | Accuracy |\n          |-----------|------------------|---------------------|----------|\n          | Walker    | 3/3 ✓            | 3/3 ✓               | 6/6=100% |\n          | Cheetah   | 3/3 ✓            | 3/3 ✓               | 6/6=100% |\n          | Cartpole  | 2/3 (1 FN)       | 3/3 ✓               | 5/6=83%  |\n          | **Total** |                  |                     | **17/18=94%** |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole NVE trajectories with 1.5x threshold line — showing gray zone cases\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cartpole 降低了 cross-env threshold accuracy：Walker+Cheetah 12/12 (100%) + Cartpole\n      5/6 (83%) = 17/18 (94%)。但如果只看 \"collapse prediction\"（nve>1.5x → 实际崩溃？），\n      accuracy 更低。Seed 0 的 nve 短暂超过 1.5x 但未崩溃 = false positive for collapse\n      prediction。论文叙事调整为：\"NVE>1.5x threshold is robust in DMC locomotion; in non-\n      locomotion tasks, the threshold may need recalibration to account for environment-specific\n      RSSM fidelity gaps\"。environments_with_confirmed_civo 维持在 2（Walker + Cheetah）。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_052\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control in non-locomotion DMC\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 200, 45K: 320, 65K: 400, 85K: 440, 105K: 470}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 0.72, 45K: 0.65, 65K: 0.55, 85K: 0.50, 105K: 0.45}\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 470\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 190, 45K: 300, 65K: 380, 85K: 420, 105K: 450}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 0.78, 45K: 0.70, 65K: 0.58, 85K: 0.52, 105K: 0.48}\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 450\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 210, 45K: 340, 65K: 420, 85K: 460, 105K: 490}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 0.68, 45K: 0.62, 65K: 0.52, 85K: 0.48, 105K: 0.42}\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 490\n      combined:\n        nve_above_1_5x_rate: \"0/3\"\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n        iqm_105K: 470\n        vs_baseline_iqm: \"-41.3%\"\n        nve_range: [0.42, 0.78]\n    result_rationale: >\n      无 dt_emb 条件下 Cartpole 与 locomotion 任务的模式一致：nve 远低于 1.5x，无崩溃。\n      有趣的是 Cartpole 的 no-dt-emb performance loss (~41%) 小于 Walker 008f (~45-84%)，\n      可能因为 Cartpole 更简单的 dynamics 对 reward prediction quality 的依赖更低。\n      这与 Cartpole 的 RSSM fidelity gap 较小的假说一致。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole trained vs no-dt-emb comparison, 3 seeds each\"\n    analysis: >\n      Causal control 在 Cartpole 也成立：no dt_emb → no CIVO (0/3 vs 1-2/3)。\n      但 Cartpole trained dt_emb 的 CIVO 本身就不清晰，所以 causal control 的 \"information\n      gain\" 低于 locomotion 任务。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # ANALYSIS EXPERIMENTS\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: \"Measure observation/reward reconstruction loss at dt=2 vs dt=1 from trained models\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline:\n        dt1_obs_mse: 13.49\n        dt2_obs_mse: 27.50\n        obs_gap: 2.04\n        dt1_reward_mae: 0.0102\n        dt2_reward_mae: 0.0159\n        reward_gap: 1.56\n      008d_trained_dtEmb:\n        dt1_obs_mse: 41.31\n        dt2_obs_mse: 53.67\n        obs_gap: 1.30\n        dt1_reward_mae: 0.0568\n        dt2_reward_mae: 0.1579\n        reward_gap: 2.78\n      008f_no_dtEmb:\n        dt1_obs_mse: 8.01\n        dt2_obs_mse: 22.04\n        obs_gap: 2.75\n        dt1_reward_mae: 0.7469\n        dt2_reward_mae: 0.7526\n        reward_gap: 1.01\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成实验的实际数据。关键发现：(1) 008d 的低 obs gap ratio (1.30x) 具有误导性——其\n      dt=1 绝对误差已是 baseline 3x（模型已崩塌时的 RSSM 质量全面恶化）；(2) 008d 的\n      reward gap 2.78x 是 CIVO 的直接 trigger——trained dt_emb 让 reward head 系统性高估\n      dt=2 transition rewards；(3) 008f 的 reward gap 1.01x 证明去掉 dt_emb 后 reward head\n      完全无法区分 dt=1/dt=2，代价是 reward_MAE 0.747（baseline 75x）。论文中必须并排报告\n      绝对误差和比率，避免审稿人被 008d 的比率误导。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"RSSM Fidelity Table\"\n        data: |\n          | Model      | dt1 obs_MSE | dt2 obs_MSE | obs gap | dt1 reward_MAE | dt2 reward_MAE | reward gap |\n          |------------|-------------|-------------|---------|----------------|----------------|------------|\n          | Baseline   | 13.49       | 27.50       | 2.04x   | 0.0102         | 0.0159         | 1.56x      |\n          | 008d       | 41.31       | 53.67       | 1.30x   | 0.0568         | 0.1579         | 2.78x      |\n          | 008f       | 8.01        | 22.04       | 2.75x   | 0.7469         | 0.7526         | 1.01x      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: absolute errors side by side with gap ratios for all 3 models\"\n    analysis: >\n      RSSM fidelity analysis 提供了 CIVO 的 mechanistic foundation。论文 Section 5 (Discussion)\n      需要用此数据解释 WHY trained dt_emb causes overestimation。\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: \"Plot actor_entropy trajectories separating healthy, CIVO-collapsed, and Pathway B configurations\"\n    expected_results:\n      healthy_configs:\n        008a_entropy_trajectory: {25K: 0.5, 35K: -1.5, 45K: -2.8, 55K: -3.5, 65K: -3.8, 75K: -4.0, 85K: -4.2, 95K: -4.3, 105K: -4.4}\n        008c_entropy_trajectory: {25K: 0.3, 35K: -0.8, 45K: -1.5, 55K: -2.0, 65K: -2.3}\n        baseline_entropy_trajectory: {25K: 0.8, 35K: -0.5, 45K: -1.8, 55K: -2.8, 65K: -3.5, 75K: -4.0, 85K: -4.3, 95K: -4.5, 105K: -4.7}\n        pattern: \"monotonic decrease (policy tightening), converging to -4.3 to -4.7\"\n      civo_collapsed:\n        008d_s0_entropy: {25K: -1.9, 35K: -3.5, 45K: -4.6, 55K: -4.9}\n        pattern: \"faster decrease than baseline, reaching lower values (more deterministic) before collapse. Entropy continues to drop even as eval collapses — actor is increasingly confident in wrong actions\"\n      pathway_b_collapsed:\n        008e_v3_s2_entropy: {55K: -5.12, 65K: -5.14, 75K: -5.22, 85K: -5.21, 95K: -4.53, 105K: -3.83}\n        pattern: \"entropy RISES during collapse (-5.21 → -3.83). Policy becomes less deterministic — actor is losing confidence, not exploiting overestimated regions\"\n      separation_metric: \"entropy_delta_at_collapse: CIVO ≈ -0.5 (decreasing), Pathway B ≈ +1.4 (increasing)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Actor entropy 是区分 Pathway A (CIVO) 和 Pathway B (non-CIVO) 的关键指标。在 CIVO 中，\n      overestimated value 驱动 actor 收敛到 (错误的) 高 value 区域——entropy 持续下降因为\n      actor 越来越 \"确定\" 该做什么（只是它确定的方向是错的）。在 Pathway B 中，policy 不稳定\n      表现为 entropy 上升——actor 失去了有效的学习信号，开始 \"犹豫\"。这个定性差异是 mechanical\n      的：CIVO 是 exploitation（信心越来越高但方向错误），Pathway B 是 destabilization\n      （信心丧失）。Healthy configs 的 entropy 单调下降到稳定值，从未反转。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Actor entropy at collapse events\"\n        data: |\n          | Config        | Entropy pre-collapse | Entropy at collapse | Δ entropy | Pattern      |\n          |---------------|---------------------|---------------------|-----------|--------------|\n          | 008d s0 (A)   | -3.47 (@35K)        | -4.88 (@55K)        | -1.41     | ↓ exploiting |\n          | 016e (A)      | -3.62 (@75K)        | -4.96 (@95K)        | -1.34     | ↓ exploiting |\n          | 008e_v3 s2 (B)| -5.21 (@85K)        | -3.83 (@105K)       | +1.38     | ↑ destabilizing |\n          | Baseline      | -4.30 (@85K)        | -4.70 (@105K)       | -0.40     | ↓ normal     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Actor entropy trajectories: healthy (green), CIVO collapse (red, entropy↓), Pathway B (orange, entropy↑)\"\n    analysis: >\n      这张图直接支持 Pathway A vs Pathway B 的 dual-mechanism 叙事。审稿人可以一眼看到两种\n      崩溃的动力学截然不同。建议放在 Figure 4 或 Figure 5 位置。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: \"Distribution plots of V(s) vs Monte Carlo return at key checkpoints\"\n    expected_results:\n      checkpoint_45K:\n        baseline:\n          value_mean: 170\n          value_std: 45\n          mc_return_mean: 514\n          mc_return_std: 120\n          overlap_fraction: 0.15\n          bias: \"conservative (V < MC)\"\n        008d_trained:\n          value_mean: 97.5\n          value_std: 80\n          mc_return_mean: 141\n          mc_return_std: 55\n          overlap_fraction: 0.35\n          bias: \"fat right tail in V(s), 20% of predictions exceed any realized return\"\n        008a_untrained:\n          value_mean: 95\n          value_std: 35\n          mc_return_mean: 563\n          mc_return_std: 100\n          overlap_fraction: 0.05\n          bias: \"strongly conservative (V << MC)\"\n        008f_no_dtEmb:\n          value_mean: 53\n          value_std: 25\n          mc_return_mean: 194\n          mc_return_std: 70\n          overlap_fraction: 0.10\n          bias: \"conservative, compressed distribution\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      V(s) distribution 比 scalar v/e ratio 提供更丰富的信息。在 CIVO configs (008d) 中，\n      V(s) 分布预期出现 fat right tail——一小部分 state 的 value 估计远超实际 MC return。\n      这些 outlier 是 actor exploitation 的 target：actor 会反复访问这些被高估的 states。\n      Untrained/no-dt-emb configs 的 V(s) 分布预期偏保守（mean V < mean MC return），没有\n      pathological right tail。Baseline 的 V(s) 分布也偏保守但 spread 更窄（well-calibrated）。\n      Median 档下，这些 distribution 在 Walker 上应很清晰，在 Cheetah 上类似但可能 noisier。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-panel violin/histogram: V(s) vs MC return at 45K for baseline, 008d, 008a, 008f\"\n      - \"Quantile-quantile plot of V(s) for 008d vs baseline showing right-tail divergence\"\n    analysis: >\n      如果时间允许，这是回应 R3 (v/e ratio is crude) 的最佳 mitigation。P2 优先级合理——\n      核心叙事不依赖此数据，但它能显著加强 C2 的 evidence quality。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: \"Analyze learned dt_embedding vectors evolution during training\"\n    expected_results:\n      init_cosine_sim_dt1_dt2: 0.15  # random init, low similarity\n      trained_008d_cosine_sim:\n        at_15K: 0.22\n        at_25K: 0.31\n        at_35K: 0.28\n        at_45K: 0.25\n        at_55K: 0.20\n        trend: \"initially diverge (dt_emb learning to distinguish dt=1/2), then partially reconverge during collapse\"\n      trained_008e_v3_s1_cosine_sim:\n        at_15K: 0.20\n        at_35K: 0.35\n        at_65K: 0.42\n        at_105K: 0.45\n        trend: \"steadily increasing similarity — dt=1 imagination means dt=2 embedding gets less gradient, converges toward dt=1\"\n      embedding_norm_ratio:\n        008d_dt2_vs_dt1: 1.35  # dt=2 embedding has larger norm\n        008e_v3_dt2_vs_dt1: 1.08  # more similar norms when dt=2 not used in imagination\n    result_rationale: >\n      dt_embedding 的 cosine similarity 揭示 model 如何 learn dt-conditioning。在 008d 中，\n      dt=1 和 dt=2 embeddings 在训练早期分化（model 学习区分两种 dt），为 CIVO 创造条件。\n      在 008e_v3 中，因为 imagination 只用 dt=1，dt=2 embedding 收到的 observation decoder\n      梯度更少，与 dt=1 embedding 逐渐趋同。Norm ratio > 1 for dt=2 说明 trained dt_emb\n      在 dt=2 处的 representation 有更大的 magnitude，可能是 overconfident prediction 的\n      geometric signature。但这些分析是 exploratory 的，不直接支持核心 claims。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cosine similarity over training: 008d vs 008e_v3, with collapse event marked\"\n    analysis: >\n      P2 优先级。如果 cosine sim trajectory 与 nve trajectory 有 correlation，可以作为\n      supplementary evidence。但不应成为论文的 critical path。\n\n  - name: \"NVE threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_034\"\n    description: \"Classification accuracy at nve thresholds 1.3x, 1.5x, 1.7x, 2.0x; AUROC\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_only:\n        threshold_1_3x: {tp: 3, fp: 1, tn: 2, fn: 0, accuracy: 0.83, note: \"009c nve=1.14x@105K is TN; 009b nve=1.24x@35K classified as FP at 1.3x if transient exceeds counted\"}\n        threshold_1_5x: {tp: 3, fp: 0, tn: 3, fn: 0, accuracy: 1.00}\n        threshold_1_7x: {tp: 2, fp: 0, tn: 3, fn: 1, accuracy: 0.83, note: \"009b peak 1.62x misclassified as negative\"}\n        threshold_2_0x: {tp: 2, fp: 0, tn: 3, fn: 1, accuracy: 0.83}\n        auroc: 0.98\n      cheetah_predicted:\n        threshold_1_5x: {tp: 3, fp: 0, tn: 3, fn: 0, accuracy: 1.00}\n        auroc: 0.96\n      cartpole_predicted:\n        threshold_1_5x: {tp: 2, fp: 0, tn: 3, fn: 1, accuracy: 0.83, note: \"seed 1 nve=1.40x is FN\"}\n        auroc: 0.89\n      cross_env_combined:\n        threshold_1_3x: {accuracy: 0.78}\n        threshold_1_5x: {accuracy: 0.94}  # 17/18 (1 FN in Cartpole)\n        threshold_1_7x: {accuracy: 0.89}\n        threshold_2_0x: {accuracy: 0.83}\n        optimal_threshold: 1.5\n        auroc: 0.95\n        cross_env_threshold_accuracy: 0.78  # weighted by environments: Walker 100%, Cheetah 100%, Cartpole 83% → (6+6+5)/18 = 94% but per-env accuracy average = (1.0+1.0+0.83)/3 = 0.94... hmm\n        note: \"Per-environment accuracy average at 1.5x: (1.0 + 1.0 + 0.83) / 3 = 0.94. However, if using only the two environments where CIVO is confirmed (Walker + Cheetah), the 'validated' accuracy is 12/12 = 100%.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档位下，1.5x 阈值是最优选择——在 Walker 和 Cheetah (locomotion) 中达到 100%\n      accuracy，在 Cartpole 中降至 83%（一个 trained seed 的 nve 停留在 gray zone 1.40x）。\n      Cross-env 总体 accuracy 94%（17/18），per-env average 94%。如果只计 \"confirmed CIVO\"\n      环境则 100%。AUROC 0.95 表明即使包含 Cartpole 的 ambiguity，NVE 仍是 strong discriminator。\n      关键 sensitivity insight：1.3x 阈值 too loose（walker 008f 的某些 seed 进入灰色地带），\n      1.7x 阈值 too strict（miss 009b 的 1.62x transient peak）。1.5x 是甜点。\n      论文中报告：(1) 1.5x threshold with 35K+ time restriction, (2) Walker+Cheetah 12/12\n      perfect, (3) Cartpole 5/6 with caveat about environment-specific calibration, (4) AUROC。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Threshold sensitivity\"\n        data: |\n          | Threshold | Walker (6) | Cheetah (6) | Cartpole (6) | Total (18) | Accuracy |\n          |-----------|------------|-------------|--------------|------------|----------|\n          | 1.3x      | 5/6        | 6/6         | 4/6          | 15/18      | 83%      |\n          | 1.5x      | 6/6        | 6/6         | 5/6          | 17/18      | 94%      |\n          | 1.7x      | 5/6        | 5/6         | 5/6          | 15/18      | 83%      |\n          | 2.0x      | 5/6        | 4/6         | 5/6          | 14/18      | 78%      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ROC curve for NVE-based CIVO detection across environments\"\n      - \"Threshold sensitivity bar chart\"\n    analysis: >\n      0 GPU cost 高 information content。必须在 submission 前完成。cross_env_threshold_accuracy\n      在 [0.67, 0.83] 的 median range 内——per-env accuracy average for environments where\n      threshold is tested is 0.94，但如果以 \"environments where threshold achieves perfect\n      separation\" 衡量则只有 2/3 = 0.67。Median 档位的 0.67-0.83 range 反映的是这个\n      \"confirmed environments / tested environments\" 比率。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # REMAINING EXPERIMENTS\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_060\"\n    description: \"Monitor RSSM prediction uncertainty during imagination, truncate when exceeding threshold\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 200, 35K: 310, 45K: 380, 55K: 420, 65K: 450, 75K: 460, 85K: 480, 95K: 500, 105K: 520}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 1.10, 45K: 1.05, 55K: 0.95, 65K: 0.88, 75K: 0.82, 85K: 0.80, 95K: 0.78, 105K: 0.75}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x: false\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 520\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-43.2%\"\n        effective_horizon: {mean: 5.2, std: 2.1, min: 2, max: 8}\n        truncation_rate: 0.35  # 35% of imagination steps are truncated\n    result_rationale: >\n      Uncertainty-gated truncation 是一个 pilot/feasibility 实验。RSSM 的 ensemble disagreement\n      或 posterior variance 在 dt>1 transitions 处应更高，truncation 会自动缩短 dt>1 的\n      effective imagination horizon。这在原理上能抑制 CIVO——model 不确定的区域被 truncated，\n      critic 不会在这些区域积累 overestimation。Median 档位下，pilot 显示 promise（nve\n      stable <1.0x, no collapse）但 performance 仅 520（57% baseline）——truncation 太 aggressive，\n      有效 horizon 被压缩到 ~5 steps（vs 原始 H=15）。需要 tuning truncation threshold，\n      但不在 CoRL deadline 范围内。论文中可作为 \"promising future direction\" 在 Section 6 讨论。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Effective horizon over training steps, showing truncation frequency\"\n    analysis: >\n      P1 优先级。如果 pilot 结果清晰（nve suppression 有效但 performance cost 高），可以\n      作为一段话放在 Discussion \"Implications for Future Work\" 中。不应作为核心 contribution。\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: \"Third DMC locomotion environment for generalization claim\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_iqm_peak: 300  # Hopper Hop is harder, DreamerV3 typically ~250-350\n      civo_trigger:\n        nve_35K_plus_range: [1.4, 2.0]\n        collapse_rate: \"1/3\"\n        note: \"Hopper dynamics are more unstable — CIVO may interact with inherent task difficulty\"\n      no_dt_emb:\n        nve_35K_plus_range: [0.5, 1.0]\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n      budget_feasibility: \"45 GPU hours = 9 × 5h experiments. P2 priority — likely deferred post-CoRL submission\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Hopper Hop 是 P2 优先级，median 档位下可能不在 CoRL deadline 前完成（GPU budget 45h\n      是所有 planned experiments 中最大的单项）。如果完成，预期结果与 Walker/Cheetah 一致\n      但可能更 noisy——Hopper 的 contact dynamics 更不稳定，baseline 本身就有较大 inter-seed\n      variance。CIVO 仍应出现（proprioceptive DMC locomotion），但 Hopper 的固有不稳定性\n      可能使 CIVO 与 task-intrinsic instability 难以区分。Median 档位的叙事不依赖 Hopper\n      数据——两环境（Walker + Cheetah）已足够支持 CoRL submission。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Hopper learning curves (if completed)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Deferred to post-submission or rebuttal. 如果 reviewer 要求第三环境，可在 rebuttal\n      期间补充。CoRL 的 rebuttal 通常有 2-3 周，足够跑完。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41456,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41456},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"744a3435-27ac-4eee-b8cf-750a0ccb367e","uuid":"466f97ef-682b-4016-8144-b7b09eae9a96"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":594069,"duration_api_ms":595809,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  CIVO mechanism confirmed in DMC locomotion (Walker Walk + Cheetah Run) with gradient-level\n  causal evidence (Full-SGS NVE=1.00×). NVE>1.5x threshold achieves perfect separation in Walker\n  (4/4) and near-perfect in Cheetah (5/6 or 6/6). Cartpole Swingup results are 'consistent with\n  but do not independently confirm' the mechanism — NVE stays in gray zone or only borderline\n  exceeds threshold, preventing a clean third-environment confirmation. Scope primary findings to\n  RSSM + proprioceptive DMC locomotion; discuss Cartpole as preliminary extension showing\n  degradation without unambiguous CIVO signature. Weaken 'generalizes across environments' to\n  'generalizes within DMC locomotion; further investigation needed for non-locomotion/visual\n  domains'. Pathway B (non-CIVO policy instability from trained dt_emb) remains under-characterized\n  — 2/4 seeds collapse across 008e_v3, mechanism identified (eval-driven, entropy↑) but causal\n  chain incomplete. Paper publishable at CoRL as strong 2-environment mechanistic diagnosis +\n  practical warning + novel TAWM contrast (MPC success vs imagination failure).\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # WALKER WALK — Multi-seed replication\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"Replicate CIVO collapse with 2 additional seeds for 008d (subsample ON + trained dt_emb + H=8)\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_009e:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 167, 35K: 146, 45K: 141, 55K: 83, 65K: 250, 75K: 178, 85K: 202, 95K: 133, 105K: 131}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 1.78, 35K: 1.71, 45K: 2.09, 55K: 4.12, 65K: 1.23, 75K: 1.48, 85K: 1.15, 95K: 1.73, 105K: 1.57}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: true\n        collapse: true\n        collapse_onset_step: 25K\n        peak_nve: 4.12\n        final_eval: 131\n      seed2_009b:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 141, 35K: 164, 45K: 141, 55K: 172, 65K: 209, 75K: 197, 85K: 236, 95K: 279, 105K: 268}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 2.05, 35K: 1.24, 45K: 1.62, 55K: 1.41, 65K: 0.94, 75K: 0.66, 85K: 0.51, 95K: 0.43, 105K: 0.38}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: true  # 1.62x@45K\n        collapse: false\n        value_self_correction: true\n        value_peak: 110.9\n        value_peak_step: 65K\n        final_eval: 268\n      combined:\n        nve_above_1_5x_rate: \"2/2\"\n        collapse_rate: \"1/2\"\n        independent_collapse_rate: 0.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档位下，Walker Walk 中 trained dt_emb 可靠触发 nve>1.5x（2/2 seeds 均超阈值），\n      但崩溃是随机的（1/2）。Seed 1 的 RSSM 在 dt=2 处产生系统性 reward 偏差（reward gap 2.78x），\n      trained dt_emb 让 critic 精确利用这个偏差，形成 value→actor→data→value 正反馈。Seed 2 同样\n      触发 nve>1.5x，但早期训练随机性（初始化、数据采样顺序）使得过度估计未能在连续 3 个 checkpoint\n      持续超过 1.5x，actor 仍能从 real returns 获得纠正梯度，value 自修正。这与 Henderson et al. 2018\n      和 Bjorck et al. 2022 的早期随机性决定训练轨迹一致。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"NVE threshold classification (Walker trained dt_emb)\"\n        data: |\n          | Seed | nve>1.5x at 35K+ | Collapse | Peak NVE | Sustained >1.5x |\n          |------|------------------|----------|----------|-----------------|\n          | 0 (008d) | ✓ (1.71x@35K) | ✓ | 4.12x | 3 checkpoints |\n          | 1 (009e) | ✓ (1.71x@35K) | ✓ | 4.12x | 3 checkpoints |\n          | 2 (009b) | ✓ (1.62x@45K) | ✗ | 2.05x | 1 checkpoint |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Learning curves: 008d seed 0+1 (collapse) vs 009b seed 2 (self-correction), overlaid with baseline\"\n      - \"NVE trajectories: 3 seeds showing all exceed 1.5x but diverge in persistence\"\n    analysis: >\n      nve>1.5x 阈值在 trained dt_emb 条件下达到 3/3（含 seed 0）完美检出率。崩溃概率 2/3\n      （seed 0 和 seed 1 崩溃，seed 2 自修正）。关键发现：sustained nve>1.5x（连续 3+\n      checkpoints）是区分崩溃 vs 自修正的第二道门。论文报告 nve>1.5x 为 necessary condition，\n      temporal persistence 为 collapse gate。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control stability with 2 additional seeds (subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8)\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_009f:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 185, 35K: 210, 45K: 195, 55K: 230, 65K: 310, 75K: 280, 85K: 350, 95K: 310, 105K: 420}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 0.95, 35K: 0.75, 45K: 0.80, 55K: 0.88, 65K: 0.45, 75K: 0.50, 85K: 0.55, 95K: 0.48, 105K: 0.35}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: false\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 420\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-54.1%\"\n      seed2_009c:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 169, 35K: 179, 45K: 211, 55K: 239, 65K: 244, 75K: 359, 85K: 227, 95K: 191, 105K: 148}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 1.26, 35K: 0.79, 45K: 0.72, 55K: 0.66, 65K: 0.53, 75K: 0.33, 85K: 0.60, 95K: 0.90, 105K: 1.14}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: false\n        collapse: false  # performance degrades but not CIVO-driven\n        final_eval: 148\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-83.8%\"\n        note: \"Decline after 75K but nve stays <1.5x; NOT delusional critic but learning instability without dt conditioning\"\n      combined:\n        nve_above_1_5x_rate: \"0/2\"\n        collapse_rate: \"0/2\"\n        cross_seed_consistency: \"Low — seed 1 recovers to 420, seed 2 declines to 148\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      去掉 dt_embedding 后，reward head 无法区分 dt=1/dt=2（reward gap 仅 1.01x），阻断了\n      CIVO 正反馈环。两个 seed 的 nve 均未超过 1.5x（max 1.26x@25K for seed 2，属于 early-stage\n      false positive zone）。但 008f 配置本身牺牲了 reward 预测质量（MAE 为 baseline 75x），\n      导致跨 seed 一致性差——seed 1 zigzag 恢复到 420（类似 seed 0 的 503），seed 2 则在 75K\n      后持续下降到 148。这种高方差归因于 reward head 噪声使 actor 学习信号质量不稳定。\n      关键论点不变：008f 是因果控制实验证明 \"without dt_emb → no CIVO\"，不是推荐方案。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"NVE threshold classification (Walker no dt_emb)\"\n        data: |\n          | Seed | nve>1.5x at 35K+ | Collapse | Peak NVE (35K+) | Final eval |\n          |------|------------------|----------|-----------------|------------|\n          | 0 (008f) | ✗ (0.97x) | ✗ | 0.97x | 503 |\n          | 1 (009f) | ✗ (0.88x) | ✗ | 0.88x | 420 |\n          | 2 (009c) | ✗ (1.14x) | ✗ | 1.14x | 148 |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"NVE trajectories: 3 seeds all below 1.5x, contrasted with 008d 3 seeds all above 1.5x\"\n    analysis: >\n      Combined with plan_011: NVE>1.5x threshold achieves 6/6 perfect classification in Walker\n      (3/3 trained exceed, 3/3 no-dt-emb below). 008f seed 2 的 nve=1.14x@105K 是最接近阈值的\n      case，但仍有 24% margin。论文中可报告 008f 跨 seed 高方差（148-503）作为 \"因果控制的代价\"，\n      与 008e_v3 seed 1 (869.9) 对比突出后者更实用。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression and zigzag recovery with 2 additional seeds (subsample OFF + untrained dt_emb + H=15)\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory: {35K: 460, 45K: 520, 55K: 440, 65K: 570, 75K: 500, 85K: 560, 95K: 610, 105K: 710}\n        nve_trajectory: {55K: 0.85, 65K: 0.62, 75K: 0.70, 85K: 0.65, 95K: 0.72, 105K: 0.55}\n        final_eval: 710\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-22.5%\"\n        zigzag_recovery: true\n        n_recovery_cycles: 2\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory: {35K: 420, 45K: 480, 55K: 410, 65K: 530, 75K: 450, 85K: 520, 95K: 550, 105K: 660}\n        nve_trajectory: {55K: 0.80, 65K: 0.58, 75K: 0.68, 85K: 0.63, 95K: 0.70, 105K: 0.52}\n        final_eval: 660\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-27.9%\"\n        zigzag_recovery: true\n        n_recovery_cycles: 2\n      combined:\n        iqm_105K: 716  # (778 + 710 + 660) / 3\n        iqm_vs_baseline: \"-21.8%\"\n        nve_range_105K: [0.52, 0.59]\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Untrained dt_emb 使 value function 无法利用精确的 dt>1 预测信息——dt_embedding 是随机固定的，\n      对 critic 来说 dt=1 和 dt=2 的 conditioning 没有语义区分。这从源头阻断了 CIVO 正反馈。\n      Median 档位下，两个新 seed 复现 seed 0 的 zigzag recovery 模式（V-shaped dips + recoveries），\n      但绝对水平略低于 seed 0（710, 660 vs 778）——这是 untrained dt_emb 配置的典型高方差特征。\n      nve 在所有 seed 中均被压制在 0.52-0.93x range，随时间进一步远离 baseline（结构性抑制，\n      非暂时延迟）。关键差异：这些 seed 的 recovery cycles 可能在 timing 上不同步，但 pattern\n      （dip → recovery → dip → higher recovery）一致，说明 zigzag 是配置的内在特征而非随机波动。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008a cross-seed summary\"\n        data: |\n          | Seed | eval@105K | nve@105K | V-recoveries | vs baseline |\n          |------|-----------|----------|--------------|-------------|\n          | 0    | 778       | 0.59x    | 2 cycles     | -15.1%      |\n          | 1    | 710       | 0.55x    | 2 cycles     | -22.5%      |\n          | 2    | 660       | 0.52x    | 2 cycles     | -27.9%      |\n          | IQM  | 716       | 0.55x    | —            | -21.8%      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-seed learning curves with shaded IQM confidence band, showing consistent zigzag pattern\"\n      - \"NVE trajectories: all 3 seeds consistently below 1.0x and declining\"\n    analysis: >\n      3-seed 数据确认 untrained dt_emb 的 value suppression 是 robust 的（0/3 collapse，nve\n      range 0.52-0.59x@105K）。IQM 716 (78% baseline) 低于 seed 0 的 778 (85%)，报告时使用\n      IQM + 95% CI 而非 best seed。C3 claim strength 保持 Strong。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 (dt=1 imag) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"Multi-seed validation of trained dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=1 imagination + H=15\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_s1:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 156, 35K: 276, 45K: 382, 55K: 487, 65K: 581, 75K: 574, 85K: 657, 95K: 852, 105K: 870}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 0.94, 45K: 0.88, 55K: 0.87, 65K: 0.72, 75K: 0.73, 85K: 0.76, 95K: 0.75, 105K: 0.80}\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 870\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-5.0%\"\n        pathway: \"healthy\"\n      seed2_s2:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 212, 35K: 320, 45K: 357, 55K: 418, 65K: 435, 75K: 577, 85K: 715, 95K: 452, 105K: 137}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 1.03, 45K: 1.06, 55K: 1.02, 65K: 0.90, 75K: 0.66, 85K: 0.68, 95K: 1.34, 105K: 3.78}\n        collapse: true\n        collapse_onset: 95K\n        collapse_type: \"Pathway B (non-CIVO, eval-driven, entropy↑)\"\n        actor_entropy_at_collapse: {85K: -5.21, 95K: -4.53, 105K: -3.83}\n        final_eval: 137\n        gate_dt_1_frac: 1.0  # dt=1 imagination never violated\n      combined:\n        collapse_rate: \"1/2\"\n        pathway_A_civo: \"0/2 (eliminated by dt=1 imagination)\"\n        pathway_B_non_civo: \"1/2\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      dt=1 imagination 消除了 Pathway A (CIVO)——imagination rollout 中不产生 dt>1 transitions，\n      critic 不会在 dt>1 处累积 overestimation。但 training data 仍含 dt>1 transitions（subsample ON），\n      trained dt_emb 仍在学习 dt=1 vs dt=2 的区分。Seed 2 的崩溃走 Pathway B：eval 先崩\n      （715→452→137），value 相对稳定（339→384→340），nve 被 eval 分母驱动而非 value 分子驱动。\n      actor_entropy 上升（-5.21→-3.83）是策略去确定化的信号，与 CIVO 的 entropy↓ 相反。\n      009a baseline s2 在同期完全稳定（618→596→836），排除 seed 2 固有脆弱假说。\n      Median 档下 Pathway B 的确切机制未完全刻画——可能是 trained dt_emb 在 representation 层面\n      引入的干扰（93% 梯度来自 observation decoders），但因果链不如 Pathway A 清晰。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008e_v3 Pathway A vs Pathway B\"\n        data: |\n          | Feature        | 008d s0 (Pathway A) | 008e_v3 s2 (Pathway B) |\n          |----------------|---------------------|------------------------|\n          | value Δ        | +130% (60→138)      | +13% (339→384)         |\n          | eval Δ         | -43% (146→83)       | -81% (715→137)         |\n          | nve driver     | value numerator     | eval denominator       |\n          | actor_entropy  | ↓ (-3.47→-4.88)     | ↑ (-5.21→-3.83)       |\n          | dt in imag     | dt=2                | dt=1 (never violated)  |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Side-by-side: 008e_v3 seed 1 (healthy) vs seed 2 (Pathway B collapse)\"\n      - \"Actor entropy comparison: CIVO collapse (↓) vs Pathway B collapse (↑)\"\n    analysis: >\n      C6 partially falsified：dt=1 imagination 消除 Pathway A 但不消除 Pathway B。崩溃率 1/2\n      与 008d (1/2-2/3) 相当——dt=1 imagination 未降低总崩溃概率。论文需将 C6 从 \"practical\n      mitigation\" 改为 \"partial mitigation (eliminates CIVO pathway only)\"。Pathway B 作为\n      open question 在 Discussion 中报告。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=2 + H=8\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"Freeze dt_embedding (requires_grad=False, random init). Diagnostic: is dt_emb TRAINING the necessary condition for CIVO?\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 172, 35K: 202, 45K: 122, 55K: 106, 65K: 160, 75K: 80, 85K: 184, 95K: 238, 105K: 204}\n        nve_trajectory: {85K: 0.47, 95K: 0.39, 105K: 0.42}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x: false\n        collapse: false\n        collapse_mechanism: \"gradient_starvation — actor_loss→0 due to frozen conditioning\"\n        actor_loss_105K: 0.000179\n        actor_entropy_105K: -4.855\n        value_mean_105K: 56.2\n        gate_dt_mean: 2.0\n        final_eval: 204\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-77.7%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Frozen dt_emb 是一个不同的失败模式：dt_embedding 固定在随机值，gate 输出恒定 dt=2，\n      但 embedding 永远不更新以匹配 RSSM dynamics。结果是 critic 收到的 conditioning 信号\n      与 state transitions 不一致，但不会产生 CIVO 的正反馈（因为 embedding 不被训练去\n      exploit RSSM 的 systematic bias）。NVE 远低于 1.0x（0.39-0.47x，critic under-estimates），\n      actor_loss→0 说明 value gradient 无法有效驱动 policy improvement。这是 gradient starvation，\n      不是 value overestimation。\n      关键论点：frozen dt_emb 确认 CIVO 需要 dt_emb 的 TRAINING——是训练过程中 observation\n      decoder 梯度（93%）塑造 dt_embedding 以 exploit RSSM fidelity gap 的能力导致了 CIVO，\n      而非 dt_embedding 的存在本身。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"dt_emb condition × CIVO outcome (Walker 2×2 matrix)\"\n        data: |\n          | dt_emb state      | Config     | NVE range  | CIVO? | Outcome         |\n          |-------------------|------------|------------|-------|-----------------|\n          | Trained           | 008d       | 1.7-4.1x   | ✓     | Collapse (2/3)  |\n          | Frozen (random)   | 015b       | 0.39-0.47x | ✗     | Grad starvation |\n          | Absent (dim=0)    | 008f       | 0.30-0.97x | ✗     | Zigzag recovery |\n          | Untrained (OFF)   | 008a       | 0.52-0.93x | ✗     | Zigzag recovery |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-way comparison: trained / frozen / absent / unexposed dt_emb learning curves\"\n    analysis: >\n      2×2 消融矩阵闭合：只有 trained + exposed to dt>1 data 的 dt_emb 触发 CIVO。Frozen 和\n      absent 都不触发，但通过不同机制失败（gradient starvation vs reward degradation）。\n      这强化了 C2: dt_emb TRAINING（而非 dt_emb 存在）是 CIVO 的 necessary condition。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 additional seeds (seed 3-4)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"Narrow 008e_v3 collapse rate estimate with 2 additional seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed3:\n        eval_trajectory: {35K: 290, 45K: 400, 55K: 510, 65K: 590, 75K: 620, 85K: 700, 95K: 820, 105K: 845}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 0.90, 45K: 0.85, 55K: 0.82, 65K: 0.70, 75K: 0.68, 85K: 0.72, 95K: 0.70, 105K: 0.75}\n        collapse: false\n        pathway: \"healthy\"\n        final_eval: 845\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-7.7%\"\n      seed4:\n        eval_trajectory: {35K: 260, 45K: 370, 55K: 450, 65K: 530, 75K: 580, 85K: 680, 95K: 420, 105K: 180}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 0.98, 45K: 0.90, 55K: 0.85, 65K: 0.75, 75K: 0.70, 85K: 0.73, 95K: 1.40, 105K: 3.20}\n        collapse: true\n        collapse_onset: 95K\n        collapse_type: \"Pathway B (non-CIVO)\"\n        actor_entropy_at_collapse: {85K: -5.15, 95K: -4.40, 105K: -3.65}\n        final_eval: 180\n      combined_all_4_seeds:\n        collapse_rate: \"2/4 (50%)\"\n        pathway_A_count: 0\n        pathway_B_count: 2\n        healthy_count: 2\n        iqm_healthy_seeds: 858  # (870 + 845) / 2\n        collapse_onset_range: \"95-105K\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档位下，008e_v3 的崩溃率稳定在 ~50%（2/4 seeds）。所有崩溃都走 Pathway B（eval-driven,\n      entropy↑），没有 Pathway A (CIVO) 出现——dt=1 imagination 有效消除了 value-driven 崩溃。\n      Pathway B 的 onset 一致在 90-100K range，晚于 Pathway A 的 25-35K onset ~70K steps。\n      这说明 Pathway B 是 slower-developing vulnerability，可能与 trained dt_emb 在 representation\n      space 中引入的 subtle bias 有关（93% 梯度来自 observation decoders 在持续塑造 dt_emb，\n      即使 imagination 不使用 dt>1）。4 seeds 不足以精确估计 collapse rate 的 CI，但 2/4\n      与 008d 的 2/3 相当，说明 dt=1 imagination 没有显著降低总崩溃概率。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008e_v3 4-seed summary\"\n        data: |\n          | Seed | eval@105K | Collapse | Pathway | Onset   |\n          |------|-----------|----------|---------|---------|\n          | 1    | 870       | ✗        | healthy | —       |\n          | 2    | 137       | ✓        | B       | 95K     |\n          | 3    | 845       | ✗        | healthy | —       |\n          | 4    | 180       | ✓        | B       | 95K     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-seed learning curves, color-coded by collapse/healthy\"\n      - \"Collapse rate comparison: 008d (2/3 CIVO) vs 008e_v3 (2/4 Pathway B)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Pathway B 在 Median 档下仍是 under-characterized。2/4 = 50% 崩溃率的 binomial 95% CI\n      是 [15%, 85%]——需要更多 seeds 才能精确估计。但方向性结论稳固：trained dt_emb + dt=1\n      imagination 不是 safe 配置。论文中 acknowledge \"Pathway B mechanism requires further\n      investigation\" 并将其作为 future work。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # CHEETAH RUN — Cross-environment replication\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in second DMC environment, establishing reference performance and v/e calibration\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 280, 45K: 480, 65K: 620, 85K: 720, 105K: 790, 155K: 830, 205K: 845, 305K: 855, 505K: 860}\n        ve_ratio_trajectory: {25K: 0.10, 45K: 0.28, 65K: 0.45, 85K: 0.58, 105K: 0.64, 155K: 0.68, 205K: 0.70}\n        peak_eval: 860\n        ve_stable_range: \"0.68-0.72 from 155K+\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 260, 45K: 460, 65K: 600, 85K: 700, 105K: 770, 155K: 820, 205K: 840, 505K: 850}\n        peak_eval: 850  # matches exp_010a actual data\n        ve_stable_range: \"0.67-0.71\"\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 300, 45K: 500, 65K: 640, 85K: 730, 105K: 800, 155K: 835, 205K: 850, 505K: 855}\n        peak_eval: 855\n        ve_stable_range: \"0.69-0.73\"\n      combined:\n        iqm_peak: 847\n        iqm_105K: 787\n        ve_stable_cross_seed: \"0.68-0.72\"\n        convergence_step: \"~155K (90% of asymptotic)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah Run 是 DMC locomotion suite 中第二标准环境。DreamerV3 在 Cheetah Run 上的 asymptotic\n      performance 略低于 Walker Walk（~850 vs ~950），因为 Cheetah 的 reward signal 更密集但\n      动力学更复杂（更多自由度的关节）。v/e calibration 与 Walker 相近（stable ~68-72%），\n      说明 DreamerV3 的 value function 在 proprioceptive DMC 任务上有一致的 overestimation\n      profile。这为 Cheetah 的 NVE 计算提供了 denominator。Seed 1 与 exp_010a 实际数据一致（849.8）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah baseline cross-seed\"\n        data: |\n          | Seed | eval@105K | Peak eval | v/e stable |\n          |------|-----------|-----------|------------|\n          | 0    | 790       | 860       | 0.68-0.72  |\n          | 1    | 770       | 850       | 0.67-0.71  |\n          | 2    | 800       | 855       | 0.69-0.73  |\n          | IQM  | 787       | 847       | 0.68-0.72  |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah baseline 3-seed learning curves with IQM band\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 稳健，cross-seed 方差小（peak range 850-860）。v/e calibration 一致。\n      为 Cheetah CIVO 实验提供可靠 reference。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: \"Replicate CIVO in Cheetah Run — key cross-environment validation\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory: {15K: 180, 25K: 320, 35K: 410, 45K: 380, 55K: 280, 65K: 150, 75K: 120}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 1.40, 35K: 1.82, 45K: 2.15, 55K: 2.48, 65K: 3.50}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: true\n        collapse: true\n        collapse_onset: 35K\n        peak_eval: 410\n        final_eval: 120\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory: {15K: 165, 25K: 290, 35K: 380, 45K: 350, 55K: 320, 65K: 350, 75K: 280, 85K: 310, 95K: 340, 105K: 370}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 1.30, 35K: 1.65, 45K: 1.48, 55K: 1.20, 65K: 0.95, 75K: 0.80, 85K: 0.72, 95K: 0.65, 105K: 0.58}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: true  # 1.65x@35K\n        collapse: false\n        value_self_correction: true\n        final_eval: 370\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-53.0%\"\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory: {15K: 190, 25K: 340, 35K: 430, 45K: 400, 55K: 310, 65K: 170, 75K: 95}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 1.50, 35K: 1.95, 45K: 2.30, 55K: 2.80, 65K: 4.10}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: true\n        collapse: true\n        collapse_onset: 35K\n        peak_eval: 430\n        final_eval: 95\n      combined:\n        nve_above_1_5x_rate: \"3/3\"\n        collapse_rate: \"2/3\"\n        cross_env_civo_collapse_rate: 0.33  # within [0.25, 0.5]\n        cheetah_civo_nve_35K_plus_range: [1.65, 2.48]  # within [1.5, 2.5]\n        iqm_all_seeds: ~195  # heavily dragged by collapsed seeds\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档位的核心预测：Cheetah 干净复制 Walker 的 CIVO 现象。RSSM 在 Cheetah 的 dt>1\n      prediction fidelity gap 与 Walker 类似（proprioceptive observations, continuous control），\n      trained dt_emb 同样触发 value overestimation feedback loop。3/3 seeds 的 nve 在 35K+\n      均超过 1.5x（range 1.65-2.48x，在 median 档的 [1.5, 2.5] 内）。崩溃率 2/3（0.33，\n      在 [0.25, 0.5] 内）。Seed 1 类似 Walker 009b 的自修正模式——nve 短暂超过 1.5x 后\n      回落。Cheetah 的 collapse onset（35K）与 Walker（25-35K）timing 相近，支持 \"RSSM\n      fidelity gap 在 35K 左右积累到临界水平\" 的机制假说。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah CIVO cross-seed\"\n        data: |\n          | Seed | nve@35K | nve@45K | Peak NVE | Collapse | Final eval |\n          |------|---------|---------|----------|----------|------------|\n          | 0    | 1.82x   | 2.15x   | 3.50x    | ✓        | 120        |\n          | 1    | 1.65x   | 1.48x   | 1.65x    | ✗        | 370        |\n          | 2    | 1.95x   | 2.30x   | 4.10x    | ✓        | 95         |\n      - name: \"Cross-environment CIVO comparison\"\n        data: |\n          | Env     | nve>1.5x rate | Collapse rate | Peak NVE range | Onset |\n          |---------|---------------|---------------|----------------|-------|\n          | Walker  | 3/3           | 2/3           | 2.05-4.12x     | 25-35K|\n          | Cheetah | 3/3           | 2/3           | 1.65-4.10x     | 35K   |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah 3-seed CIVO learning curves, overlaid with Walker 008d for cross-env comparison\"\n      - \"NVE trajectories: Cheetah 3 seeds, with 1.5x threshold line\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 复制是论文最重要的新增证据。nve>1.5x 阈值在 Cheetah 也实现 3/3 检出。\n      Combined Walker + Cheetah: trained dt_emb 6/6 超 1.5x (100%)。论文可 claim \"CIVO\n      mechanism confirmed in DMC locomotion\"。崩溃率跨环境一致 (~50-67%)，支持 \"CIVO 是\n      necessary condition, collapse stochastic\" 的叙事。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control (no dt_embedding → no CIVO) in Cheetah Run\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 170, 35K: 200, 45K: 220, 55K: 240, 65K: 300, 75K: 280, 85K: 310, 95K: 350, 105K: 380}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 0.90, 35K: 0.70, 45K: 0.75, 55K: 0.82, 65K: 0.50, 75K: 0.55, 85K: 0.60, 95K: 0.52, 105K: 0.45}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: false\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 380\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-51.9%\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 155, 35K: 190, 45K: 210, 55K: 195, 65K: 260, 75K: 240, 85K: 270, 95K: 300, 105K: 330}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 0.80, 45K: 0.68, 55K: 0.90, 65K: 0.55, 85K: 0.70, 105K: 0.55}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: false\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 330\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 180, 35K: 215, 45K: 240, 55K: 260, 65K: 320, 75K: 310, 85K: 340, 95K: 370, 105K: 400}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 0.65, 45K: 0.72, 55K: 0.78, 65K: 0.48, 85K: 0.58, 105K: 0.40}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: false\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 400\n      combined:\n        nve_above_1_5x_rate: \"0/3\"\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n        cheetah_no_dt_emb_nve_35K_plus_range: [0.40, 0.90]  # within [0.4, 1.1]\n        iqm_105K: 370\n        vs_baseline_iqm: \"-53.0%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 Walker 008f 的模式一致：去掉 dt_embedding 后 reward head 无法区分 dt=1/dt=2，\n      阻断 CIVO 正反馈。所有 3 seeds 的 nve 在 35K+ 范围内为 0.40-0.90x（在 median 档的\n      [0.4, 1.1] 内），无 seed 超过 1.5x。性能损失约 50%（与 Walker 008f 的 45-84% 损失\n      range 一致），归因于 reward prediction degradation。Cheetah 与 Walker 的因果控制\n      结论一致：no dt_emb → no CIVO。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah no-dt-emb cross-seed\"\n        data: |\n          | Seed | nve max (35K+) | Collapse | eval@105K | vs baseline |\n          |------|----------------|----------|-----------|-------------|\n          | 0    | 0.82x          | ✗        | 380       | -51.9%      |\n          | 1    | 0.90x          | ✗        | 330       | -58.2%      |\n          | 2    | 0.78x          | ✗        | 400       | -49.4%      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah no-dt-emb NVE trajectories contrasted with trained dt_emb (plan_021)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Combined with plan_021: Cheetah NVE threshold classification = 6/6 (3/3 trained exceed,\n      3/3 no-dt-emb below). Cross-environment NVE threshold total: Walker 6/6 + Cheetah 6/6\n      = 12/12 (100%). 论文可 claim \"NVE>1.5x is a reliable cross-environment diagnostic\n      for trained dt_emb CIVO in DMC locomotion\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression pattern in Cheetah\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory: {35K: 380, 45K: 440, 55K: 400, 65K: 490, 75K: 460, 85K: 520, 95K: 540, 105K: 620}\n        nve_trajectory: {55K: 0.78, 65K: 0.60, 75K: 0.65, 85K: 0.62, 95K: 0.68, 105K: 0.55}\n        final_eval: 620\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-21.4%\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory: {35K: 350, 45K: 410, 55K: 380, 65K: 460, 75K: 430, 85K: 490, 95K: 510, 105K: 580}\n        nve_trajectory: {55K: 0.82, 65K: 0.63, 75K: 0.70, 85K: 0.65, 95K: 0.72, 105K: 0.58}\n        final_eval: 580\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-26.5%\"\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory: {35K: 400, 45K: 470, 55K: 420, 65K: 520, 75K: 490, 85K: 550, 95K: 570, 105K: 650}\n        nve_trajectory: {55K: 0.75, 65K: 0.57, 75K: 0.63, 85K: 0.60, 95K: 0.65, 105K: 0.52}\n        final_eval: 650\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-17.6%\"\n      combined:\n        iqm_105K: 617\n        vs_baseline_iqm: \"-21.8%\"\n        nve_range_105K: [0.52, 0.58]\n        zigzag_recovery: \"2/3 seeds show at least 1 V-recovery cycle\"\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 Walker 008a 模式一致：untrained dt_emb 阻断 CIVO 但保留了完整的 model architecture\n      （包括 dt_embedding 参数，只是不更新权重 exposed to dt>1 data）。Value function 无法\n      exploit dt-specific conditioning，nve 被压制在 0.52-0.82x range。Zigzag recovery 模式\n      在 Cheetah 中也出现，但幅度可能略小（Cheetah 的 observation space 更大，learning 更\n      noisy）。IQM 617 (78% baseline) 与 Walker 008a 的 IQM 716 (78% baseline) 百分比一致，\n      说明 untrained dt_emb 的 \"代价\" 是跨环境稳定的 ~20% performance loss。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah untrained dt_emb learning curves, contrasted with trained (plan_021) and no-dt-emb (plan_022)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 确认 untrained dt_emb 的 value suppression 是跨环境 robust 的。\n      与 plan_021/022 合并：Cheetah 完整复制 Walker 的 CIVO 因果链。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # CARTPOLE SWINGUP — Third environment (borderline in median)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_050\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in non-locomotion DMC environment\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 300, 45K: 540, 65K: 680, 85K: 760, 105K: 800, 155K: 830, 205K: 845, 505K: 855}\n        peak_eval: 855\n        ve_stable_range: \"0.65-0.70\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 280, 45K: 520, 65K: 660, 85K: 740, 105K: 790, 155K: 825, 505K: 850}\n        peak_eval: 850\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 320, 45K: 560, 65K: 700, 85K: 770, 105K: 810, 155K: 840, 505K: 860}\n        peak_eval: 860\n      combined:\n        iqm_peak: 855\n        iqm_105K: 800\n        ve_stable_cross_seed: \"0.65-0.71\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole Swingup 是 DMC 非 locomotion 任务。DreamerV3 在此环境 asymptotic ~850-860，\n      略低于 Walker (~950) 但与 Cheetah 相近。v/e calibration 与 locomotion 任务相似\n      （0.65-0.71），说明 DreamerV3 的 value overestimation profile 在 proprioceptive\n      DMC 任务间相对一致。Cartpole 的 observation space 比 locomotion 更简单（仅 cart position,\n      velocity, pole angle, angular velocity），这可能影响 RSSM 在 dt>1 处的 fidelity gap\n      大小——简单 dynamics 可能让 RSSM 在 dt>1 处也能保持较好精度。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole baseline 3-seed learning curves\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 稳健。关键不确定性：Cartpole 更简单的 dynamics 是否会减小 RSSM fidelity gap，\n      从而削弱 CIVO 的 intensity。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_051\"\n    description: \"Test CIVO in non-locomotion DMC environment\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory: {15K: 160, 25K: 310, 35K: 420, 45K: 380, 55K: 350, 65K: 320, 75K: 290, 85K: 280, 95K: 270, 105K: 260}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 1.20, 35K: 1.42, 45K: 1.55, 55K: 1.48, 65K: 1.35, 75K: 1.30, 85K: 1.25, 95K: 1.20, 105K: 1.15}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: true  # 1.55x@45K but transient\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 260\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-67.5%\"\n        note: \"NVE briefly exceeds 1.5x at 45K but does not sustain\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory: {15K: 150, 25K: 290, 35K: 400, 45K: 370, 55K: 340, 65K: 310, 75K: 350, 85K: 320, 95K: 340, 105K: 310}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 1.10, 35K: 1.35, 45K: 1.40, 55K: 1.32, 65K: 1.25, 75K: 1.10, 85K: 1.05, 95K: 1.00, 105K: 0.95}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: false  # max 1.40x — below threshold\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 310\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory: {15K: 170, 25K: 330, 35K: 440, 45K: 410, 55K: 350, 65K: 180, 75K: 140}\n        nve_trajectory: {25K: 1.30, 35K: 1.60, 45K: 1.85, 55K: 2.10, 65K: 2.80}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x_at_35K_plus: true\n        collapse: true\n        collapse_onset: 45K\n        final_eval: 140\n      combined:\n        nve_above_1_5x_rate: \"2/3\"\n        collapse_rate: \"1/3\"\n        nve_35K_plus_range: [0.95, 2.80]\n        threshold_1_5x_classification: \"2/3 correctly classified (seed 1 = false negative: trained dt_emb but nve<1.5x)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档位下 Cartpole 的 CIVO 表现不如 locomotion 任务清晰。原因：Cartpole 的 dynamics\n      更简单（4-dim state vs Walker 的 24-dim），RSSM 在 dt>1 处的 prediction error 较小，\n      导致 reward gap ratio 不如 Walker/Cheetah 大。结果是 nve 整体偏低（部分 seed 的 nve\n      在 1.3-1.5x 的灰色地带），1.5x 阈值在 Cartpole 上出现 false negative（seed 1 有\n      trained dt_emb 但 nve 仅 1.40x）。只有 1/3 seeds 崩溃——相比 Walker/Cheetah 的 ~50-67%\n      明显更低。这导致 Cartpole 不能被计入 \"confirmed CIVO\" 环境，只能说 \"consistent with CIVO\n      but threshold may need environment-specific calibration\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole CIVO cross-seed\"\n        data: |\n          | Seed | nve max (35K+) | >1.5x? | Collapse | Final eval |\n          |------|----------------|--------|----------|------------|\n          | 0    | 1.55x          | ✓ (transient) | ✗ | 260        |\n          | 1    | 1.40x          | ✗ (gray zone) | ✗ | 310        |\n          | 2    | 2.80x          | ✓      | ✓        | 140        |\n      - name: \"NVE threshold accuracy: cross-environment\"\n        data: |\n          | Env       | Trained (>1.5x?) | No-dt-emb (<1.5x?) | Accuracy |\n          |-----------|------------------|---------------------|----------|\n          | Walker    | 3/3 ✓            | 3/3 ✓               | 6/6=100% |\n          | Cheetah   | 3/3 ✓            | 3/3 ✓               | 6/6=100% |\n          | Cartpole  | 2/3 (1 FN)       | 3/3 ✓               | 5/6=83%  |\n          | **Total** |                  |                     | **17/18=94%** |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole NVE trajectories with 1.5x threshold line — showing gray zone cases\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cartpole 降低了 cross-env threshold accuracy：Walker+Cheetah 12/12 (100%) + Cartpole\n      5/6 (83%) = 17/18 (94%)。但如果只看 \"collapse prediction\"（nve>1.5x → 实际崩溃？），\n      accuracy 更低。Seed 0 的 nve 短暂超过 1.5x 但未崩溃 = false positive for collapse\n      prediction。论文叙事调整为：\"NVE>1.5x threshold is robust in DMC locomotion; in non-\n      locomotion tasks, the threshold may need recalibration to account for environment-specific\n      RSSM fidelity gaps\"。environments_with_confirmed_civo 维持在 2（Walker + Cheetah）。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_052\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control in non-locomotion DMC\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 200, 45K: 320, 65K: 400, 85K: 440, 105K: 470}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 0.72, 45K: 0.65, 65K: 0.55, 85K: 0.50, 105K: 0.45}\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 470\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 190, 45K: 300, 65K: 380, 85K: 420, 105K: 450}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 0.78, 45K: 0.70, 65K: 0.58, 85K: 0.52, 105K: 0.48}\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 450\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 210, 45K: 340, 65K: 420, 85K: 460, 105K: 490}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 0.68, 45K: 0.62, 65K: 0.52, 85K: 0.48, 105K: 0.42}\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 490\n      combined:\n        nve_above_1_5x_rate: \"0/3\"\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n        iqm_105K: 470\n        vs_baseline_iqm: \"-41.3%\"\n        nve_range: [0.42, 0.78]\n    result_rationale: >\n      无 dt_emb 条件下 Cartpole 与 locomotion 任务的模式一致：nve 远低于 1.5x，无崩溃。\n      有趣的是 Cartpole 的 no-dt-emb performance loss (~41%) 小于 Walker 008f (~45-84%)，\n      可能因为 Cartpole 更简单的 dynamics 对 reward prediction quality 的依赖更低。\n      这与 Cartpole 的 RSSM fidelity gap 较小的假说一致。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole trained vs no-dt-emb comparison, 3 seeds each\"\n    analysis: >\n      Causal control 在 Cartpole 也成立：no dt_emb → no CIVO (0/3 vs 1-2/3)。\n      但 Cartpole trained dt_emb 的 CIVO 本身就不清晰，所以 causal control 的 \"information\n      gain\" 低于 locomotion 任务。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # ANALYSIS EXPERIMENTS\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: \"Measure observation/reward reconstruction loss at dt=2 vs dt=1 from trained models\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline:\n        dt1_obs_mse: 13.49\n        dt2_obs_mse: 27.50\n        obs_gap: 2.04\n        dt1_reward_mae: 0.0102\n        dt2_reward_mae: 0.0159\n        reward_gap: 1.56\n      008d_trained_dtEmb:\n        dt1_obs_mse: 41.31\n        dt2_obs_mse: 53.67\n        obs_gap: 1.30\n        dt1_reward_mae: 0.0568\n        dt2_reward_mae: 0.1579\n        reward_gap: 2.78\n      008f_no_dtEmb:\n        dt1_obs_mse: 8.01\n        dt2_obs_mse: 22.04\n        obs_gap: 2.75\n        dt1_reward_mae: 0.7469\n        dt2_reward_mae: 0.7526\n        reward_gap: 1.01\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成实验的实际数据。关键发现：(1) 008d 的低 obs gap ratio (1.30x) 具有误导性——其\n      dt=1 绝对误差已是 baseline 3x（模型已崩塌时的 RSSM 质量全面恶化）；(2) 008d 的\n      reward gap 2.78x 是 CIVO 的直接 trigger——trained dt_emb 让 reward head 系统性高估\n      dt=2 transition rewards；(3) 008f 的 reward gap 1.01x 证明去掉 dt_emb 后 reward head\n      完全无法区分 dt=1/dt=2，代价是 reward_MAE 0.747（baseline 75x）。论文中必须并排报告\n      绝对误差和比率，避免审稿人被 008d 的比率误导。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"RSSM Fidelity Table\"\n        data: |\n          | Model      | dt1 obs_MSE | dt2 obs_MSE | obs gap | dt1 reward_MAE | dt2 reward_MAE | reward gap |\n          |------------|-------------|-------------|---------|----------------|----------------|------------|\n          | Baseline   | 13.49       | 27.50       | 2.04x   | 0.0102         | 0.0159         | 1.56x      |\n          | 008d       | 41.31       | 53.67       | 1.30x   | 0.0568         | 0.1579         | 2.78x      |\n          | 008f       | 8.01        | 22.04       | 2.75x   | 0.7469         | 0.7526         | 1.01x      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: absolute errors side by side with gap ratios for all 3 models\"\n    analysis: >\n      RSSM fidelity analysis 提供了 CIVO 的 mechanistic foundation。论文 Section 5 (Discussion)\n      需要用此数据解释 WHY trained dt_emb causes overestimation。\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: \"Plot actor_entropy trajectories separating healthy, CIVO-collapsed, and Pathway B configurations\"\n    expected_results:\n      healthy_configs:\n        008a_entropy_trajectory: {25K: 0.5, 35K: -1.5, 45K: -2.8, 55K: -3.5, 65K: -3.8, 75K: -4.0, 85K: -4.2, 95K: -4.3, 105K: -4.4}\n        008c_entropy_trajectory: {25K: 0.3, 35K: -0.8, 45K: -1.5, 55K: -2.0, 65K: -2.3}\n        baseline_entropy_trajectory: {25K: 0.8, 35K: -0.5, 45K: -1.8, 55K: -2.8, 65K: -3.5, 75K: -4.0, 85K: -4.3, 95K: -4.5, 105K: -4.7}\n        pattern: \"monotonic decrease (policy tightening), converging to -4.3 to -4.7\"\n      civo_collapsed:\n        008d_s0_entropy: {25K: -1.9, 35K: -3.5, 45K: -4.6, 55K: -4.9}\n        pattern: \"faster decrease than baseline, reaching lower values (more deterministic) before collapse. Entropy continues to drop even as eval collapses — actor is increasingly confident in wrong actions\"\n      pathway_b_collapsed:\n        008e_v3_s2_entropy: {55K: -5.12, 65K: -5.14, 75K: -5.22, 85K: -5.21, 95K: -4.53, 105K: -3.83}\n        pattern: \"entropy RISES during collapse (-5.21 → -3.83). Policy becomes less deterministic — actor is losing confidence, not exploiting overestimated regions\"\n      separation_metric: \"entropy_delta_at_collapse: CIVO ≈ -0.5 (decreasing), Pathway B ≈ +1.4 (increasing)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Actor entropy 是区分 Pathway A (CIVO) 和 Pathway B (non-CIVO) 的关键指标。在 CIVO 中，\n      overestimated value 驱动 actor 收敛到 (错误的) 高 value 区域——entropy 持续下降因为\n      actor 越来越 \"确定\" 该做什么（只是它确定的方向是错的）。在 Pathway B 中，policy 不稳定\n      表现为 entropy 上升——actor 失去了有效的学习信号，开始 \"犹豫\"。这个定性差异是 mechanical\n      的：CIVO 是 exploitation（信心越来越高但方向错误），Pathway B 是 destabilization\n      （信心丧失）。Healthy configs 的 entropy 单调下降到稳定值，从未反转。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Actor entropy at collapse events\"\n        data: |\n          | Config        | Entropy pre-collapse | Entropy at collapse | Δ entropy | Pattern      |\n          |---------------|---------------------|---------------------|-----------|--------------|\n          | 008d s0 (A)   | -3.47 (@35K)        | -4.88 (@55K)        | -1.41     | ↓ exploiting |\n          | 016e (A)      | -3.62 (@75K)        | -4.96 (@95K)        | -1.34     | ↓ exploiting |\n          | 008e_v3 s2 (B)| -5.21 (@85K)        | -3.83 (@105K)       | +1.38     | ↑ destabilizing |\n          | Baseline      | -4.30 (@85K)        | -4.70 (@105K)       | -0.40     | ↓ normal     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Actor entropy trajectories: healthy (green), CIVO collapse (red, entropy↓), Pathway B (orange, entropy↑)\"\n    analysis: >\n      这张图直接支持 Pathway A vs Pathway B 的 dual-mechanism 叙事。审稿人可以一眼看到两种\n      崩溃的动力学截然不同。建议放在 Figure 4 或 Figure 5 位置。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: \"Distribution plots of V(s) vs Monte Carlo return at key checkpoints\"\n    expected_results:\n      checkpoint_45K:\n        baseline:\n          value_mean: 170\n          value_std: 45\n          mc_return_mean: 514\n          mc_return_std: 120\n          overlap_fraction: 0.15\n          bias: \"conservative (V < MC)\"\n        008d_trained:\n          value_mean: 97.5\n          value_std: 80\n          mc_return_mean: 141\n          mc_return_std: 55\n          overlap_fraction: 0.35\n          bias: \"fat right tail in V(s), 20% of predictions exceed any realized return\"\n        008a_untrained:\n          value_mean: 95\n          value_std: 35\n          mc_return_mean: 563\n          mc_return_std: 100\n          overlap_fraction: 0.05\n          bias: \"strongly conservative (V << MC)\"\n        008f_no_dtEmb:\n          value_mean: 53\n          value_std: 25\n          mc_return_mean: 194\n          mc_return_std: 70\n          overlap_fraction: 0.10\n          bias: \"conservative, compressed distribution\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      V(s) distribution 比 scalar v/e ratio 提供更丰富的信息。在 CIVO configs (008d) 中，\n      V(s) 分布预期出现 fat right tail——一小部分 state 的 value 估计远超实际 MC return。\n      这些 outlier 是 actor exploitation 的 target：actor 会反复访问这些被高估的 states。\n      Untrained/no-dt-emb configs 的 V(s) 分布预期偏保守（mean V < mean MC return），没有\n      pathological right tail。Baseline 的 V(s) 分布也偏保守但 spread 更窄（well-calibrated）。\n      Median 档下，这些 distribution 在 Walker 上应很清晰，在 Cheetah 上类似但可能 noisier。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-panel violin/histogram: V(s) vs MC return at 45K for baseline, 008d, 008a, 008f\"\n      - \"Quantile-quantile plot of V(s) for 008d vs baseline showing right-tail divergence\"\n    analysis: >\n      如果时间允许，这是回应 R3 (v/e ratio is crude) 的最佳 mitigation。P2 优先级合理——\n      核心叙事不依赖此数据，但它能显著加强 C2 的 evidence quality。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: \"Analyze learned dt_embedding vectors evolution during training\"\n    expected_results:\n      init_cosine_sim_dt1_dt2: 0.15  # random init, low similarity\n      trained_008d_cosine_sim:\n        at_15K: 0.22\n        at_25K: 0.31\n        at_35K: 0.28\n        at_45K: 0.25\n        at_55K: 0.20\n        trend: \"initially diverge (dt_emb learning to distinguish dt=1/2), then partially reconverge during collapse\"\n      trained_008e_v3_s1_cosine_sim:\n        at_15K: 0.20\n        at_35K: 0.35\n        at_65K: 0.42\n        at_105K: 0.45\n        trend: \"steadily increasing similarity — dt=1 imagination means dt=2 embedding gets less gradient, converges toward dt=1\"\n      embedding_norm_ratio:\n        008d_dt2_vs_dt1: 1.35  # dt=2 embedding has larger norm\n        008e_v3_dt2_vs_dt1: 1.08  # more similar norms when dt=2 not used in imagination\n    result_rationale: >\n      dt_embedding 的 cosine similarity 揭示 model 如何 learn dt-conditioning。在 008d 中，\n      dt=1 和 dt=2 embeddings 在训练早期分化（model 学习区分两种 dt），为 CIVO 创造条件。\n      在 008e_v3 中，因为 imagination 只用 dt=1，dt=2 embedding 收到的 observation decoder\n      梯度更少，与 dt=1 embedding 逐渐趋同。Norm ratio > 1 for dt=2 说明 trained dt_emb\n      在 dt=2 处的 representation 有更大的 magnitude，可能是 overconfident prediction 的\n      geometric signature。但这些分析是 exploratory 的，不直接支持核心 claims。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cosine similarity over training: 008d vs 008e_v3, with collapse event marked\"\n    analysis: >\n      P2 优先级。如果 cosine sim trajectory 与 nve trajectory 有 correlation，可以作为\n      supplementary evidence。但不应成为论文的 critical path。\n\n  - name: \"NVE threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_034\"\n    description: \"Classification accuracy at nve thresholds 1.3x, 1.5x, 1.7x, 2.0x; AUROC\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_only:\n        threshold_1_3x: {tp: 3, fp: 1, tn: 2, fn: 0, accuracy: 0.83, note: \"009c nve=1.14x@105K is TN; 009b nve=1.24x@35K classified as FP at 1.3x if transient exceeds counted\"}\n        threshold_1_5x: {tp: 3, fp: 0, tn: 3, fn: 0, accuracy: 1.00}\n        threshold_1_7x: {tp: 2, fp: 0, tn: 3, fn: 1, accuracy: 0.83, note: \"009b peak 1.62x misclassified as negative\"}\n        threshold_2_0x: {tp: 2, fp: 0, tn: 3, fn: 1, accuracy: 0.83}\n        auroc: 0.98\n      cheetah_predicted:\n        threshold_1_5x: {tp: 3, fp: 0, tn: 3, fn: 0, accuracy: 1.00}\n        auroc: 0.96\n      cartpole_predicted:\n        threshold_1_5x: {tp: 2, fp: 0, tn: 3, fn: 1, accuracy: 0.83, note: \"seed 1 nve=1.40x is FN\"}\n        auroc: 0.89\n      cross_env_combined:\n        threshold_1_3x: {accuracy: 0.78}\n        threshold_1_5x: {accuracy: 0.94}  # 17/18 (1 FN in Cartpole)\n        threshold_1_7x: {accuracy: 0.89}\n        threshold_2_0x: {accuracy: 0.83}\n        optimal_threshold: 1.5\n        auroc: 0.95\n        cross_env_threshold_accuracy: 0.78  # weighted by environments: Walker 100%, Cheetah 100%, Cartpole 83% → (6+6+5)/18 = 94% but per-env accuracy average = (1.0+1.0+0.83)/3 = 0.94... hmm\n        note: \"Per-environment accuracy average at 1.5x: (1.0 + 1.0 + 0.83) / 3 = 0.94. However, if using only the two environments where CIVO is confirmed (Walker + Cheetah), the 'validated' accuracy is 12/12 = 100%.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档位下，1.5x 阈值是最优选择——在 Walker 和 Cheetah (locomotion) 中达到 100%\n      accuracy，在 Cartpole 中降至 83%（一个 trained seed 的 nve 停留在 gray zone 1.40x）。\n      Cross-env 总体 accuracy 94%（17/18），per-env average 94%。如果只计 \"confirmed CIVO\"\n      环境则 100%。AUROC 0.95 表明即使包含 Cartpole 的 ambiguity，NVE 仍是 strong discriminator。\n      关键 sensitivity insight：1.3x 阈值 too loose（walker 008f 的某些 seed 进入灰色地带），\n      1.7x 阈值 too strict（miss 009b 的 1.62x transient peak）。1.5x 是甜点。\n      论文中报告：(1) 1.5x threshold with 35K+ time restriction, (2) Walker+Cheetah 12/12\n      perfect, (3) Cartpole 5/6 with caveat about environment-specific calibration, (4) AUROC。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Threshold sensitivity\"\n        data: |\n          | Threshold | Walker (6) | Cheetah (6) | Cartpole (6) | Total (18) | Accuracy |\n          |-----------|------------|-------------|--------------|------------|----------|\n          | 1.3x      | 5/6        | 6/6         | 4/6          | 15/18      | 83%      |\n          | 1.5x      | 6/6        | 6/6         | 5/6          | 17/18      | 94%      |\n          | 1.7x      | 5/6        | 5/6         | 5/6          | 15/18      | 83%      |\n          | 2.0x      | 5/6        | 4/6         | 5/6          | 14/18      | 78%      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ROC curve for NVE-based CIVO detection across environments\"\n      - \"Threshold sensitivity bar chart\"\n    analysis: >\n      0 GPU cost 高 information content。必须在 submission 前完成。cross_env_threshold_accuracy\n      在 [0.67, 0.83] 的 median range 内——per-env accuracy average for environments where\n      threshold is tested is 0.94，但如果以 \"environments where threshold achieves perfect\n      separation\" 衡量则只有 2/3 = 0.67。Median 档位的 0.67-0.83 range 反映的是这个\n      \"confirmed environments / tested environments\" 比率。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # REMAINING EXPERIMENTS\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_060\"\n    description: \"Monitor RSSM prediction uncertainty during imagination, truncate when exceeding threshold\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory: {25K: 200, 35K: 310, 45K: 380, 55K: 420, 65K: 450, 75K: 460, 85K: 480, 95K: 500, 105K: 520}\n        nve_trajectory: {35K: 1.10, 45K: 1.05, 55K: 0.95, 65K: 0.88, 75K: 0.82, 85K: 0.80, 95K: 0.78, 105K: 0.75}\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x: false\n        collapse: false\n        final_eval: 520\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-43.2%\"\n        effective_horizon: {mean: 5.2, std: 2.1, min: 2, max: 8}\n        truncation_rate: 0.35  # 35% of imagination steps are truncated\n    result_rationale: >\n      Uncertainty-gated truncation 是一个 pilot/feasibility 实验。RSSM 的 ensemble disagreement\n      或 posterior variance 在 dt>1 transitions 处应更高，truncation 会自动缩短 dt>1 的\n      effective imagination horizon。这在原理上能抑制 CIVO——model 不确定的区域被 truncated，\n      critic 不会在这些区域积累 overestimation。Median 档位下，pilot 显示 promise（nve\n      stable <1.0x, no collapse）但 performance 仅 520（57% baseline）——truncation 太 aggressive，\n      有效 horizon 被压缩到 ~5 steps（vs 原始 H=15）。需要 tuning truncation threshold，\n      但不在 CoRL deadline 范围内。论文中可作为 \"promising future direction\" 在 Section 6 讨论。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Effective horizon over training steps, showing truncation frequency\"\n    analysis: >\n      P1 优先级。如果 pilot 结果清晰（nve suppression 有效但 performance cost 高），可以\n      作为一段话放在 Discussion \"Implications for Future Work\" 中。不应作为核心 contribution。\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: \"Third DMC locomotion environment for generalization claim\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_iqm_peak: 300  # Hopper Hop is harder, DreamerV3 typically ~250-350\n      civo_trigger:\n        nve_35K_plus_range: [1.4, 2.0]\n        collapse_rate: \"1/3\"\n        note: \"Hopper dynamics are more unstable — CIVO may interact with inherent task difficulty\"\n      no_dt_emb:\n        nve_35K_plus_range: [0.5, 1.0]\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n      budget_feasibility: \"45 GPU hours = 9 × 5h experiments. P2 priority — likely deferred post-CoRL submission\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Hopper Hop 是 P2 优先级，median 档位下可能不在 CoRL deadline 前完成（GPU budget 45h\n      是所有 planned experiments 中最大的单项）。如果完成，预期结果与 Walker/Cheetah 一致\n      但可能更 noisy——Hopper 的 contact dynamics 更不稳定，baseline 本身就有较大 inter-seed\n      variance。CIVO 仍应出现（proprioceptive DMC locomotion），但 Hopper 的固有不稳定性\n      可能使 CIVO 与 task-intrinsic instability 难以区分。Median 档位的叙事不依赖 Hopper\n      数据——两环境（Walker + Cheetah）已足够支持 CoRL submission。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Hopper learning curves (if completed)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Deferred to post-submission or rebuttal. 如果 reviewer 要求第三环境，可在 rebuttal\n      期间补充。CoRL 的 rebuttal 通常有 2-3 周，足够跑完。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"744a3435-27ac-4eee-b8cf-750a0ccb367e","total_cost_usd":1.1451665,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41456,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"output_tokens":33769,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41456,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":33769,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41456,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41456},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":36013,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.036108,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":33769,"cacheReadInputTokens":11447,"cacheCreationInputTokens":41456,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.1090585,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"6baf4f3a-6d65-46b1-ba67-423c1a9ab86b"}
